{"Target":{"Guid":"ac0f0857-665c-469d-8080-956d95610e16","Ancestry":[{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<wnd app=\"msedge.exe\" cls=\"Chrome_WidgetWin_1\" title=\"Oppl&#xE6;ringsadministrasjon og 2 sider til &#x2013; [InPrivate] &#x2013; Microsof*\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"app":"msedge.exe","cls":"Chrome_WidgetWin_1","title":"Opplæringsadministrasjon og 2 sider til – [InPrivate] – Microsof*","aastate":"skalerbar, flyttbar, fokuserbar"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl name=\"Oppl&#xE6;ringsadministrasjon\" role=\"document\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"name":"Opplæringsadministrasjon","role":"document","aastate":"skrivebeskyttet, fokuserbar, opaque","text":"https://dfohrsandbox-stage.lms.hr.cloud.sap/learning/admin/theming/updateThemingInfo.do?4102444799=0#/learning/iframeApp@/loadPageInIframe//%252Flearning%252Fadmin%252Fsysadmin%252FviewSystemConfigurationList.do%253FadminShellMenuId%253DsystemConfiguration%2526adminShellMenuId%253DsystemConfiguration%2526adminShellMenuId%253DsystemConfiguration%2526adminShellMenuId%253DsystemConfiguration"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl name=\"Systemkonfigurasjon\" role=\"document\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"name":"Systemkonfigurasjon","role":"document","aastate":"opaque"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl name=\"Systemadministrasjon &gt; Konfigurasjon &gt; Systemkonfigurasjon &gt; Sam*\" role=\"document\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"name":"Systemadministrasjon > Konfigurasjon > Systemkonfigurasjon > Sam*","role":"document","aastate":"har fokus, skrivebeskyttet, fokuserbar, opaque","text":"https://dfohrsandbox-stage.lms.hr.cloud.sap/learning/admin/sysadmin/editConfigurationSummary.do?configID=com%2eplateausystems%2eelms%2eframework%2econfiguration%2econfigurations%2eElmsConfiguration"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl role=\"row\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"role":"row","aastate":"opaque","rowName":"Systemkonfigurasjon  |  | Hjelp  > Rediger systemkonfigurasjon     Konfigurasjons-ID : LMS_ADMIN  Beskrivelse : Denne konfigurasjonen inneholder systemadministratorinformasjon som er påkrevd for å kunne tilpasse ELMS-programmet.     Rediger systemkonfigurasjon  Bruk endringer Tilbakestill  : Konfigurasjon  # This configuration contains system administrator information required to configure the Talent Management application. # It is divided into sections to group the concerns: #    SYSTEM: Contains settings for TMS Globally (and not a particular module) #    I18N BEHAVIOR: Contains settings for the internationalization system of Talent Management #    HELP SYSTEM: Contains settings for the help system of Talent Management #    LEARNING CONTENT: Contains settings for the delivery of learning content to users #    BACKGROUND JOB: Contains settings for background job processing #    ALL USERS/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS: Contains settings to control how all users (both admin and end) interact with the application #    END USERS/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS: Contains settings to control how end users interact with the application #    ADMIN/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS: Contains settings to control how administrators interact with the application # **************************************** # *********** SYSTEM SETTINGS ************ # **************************************** # **** System Settings: Encryption Settings **** # The following encryption uses the JavaTM Cryptography Architecture. # Changing any of these values will cause all encrypted data in the database to be re-encrypted using the new settings. # See the documentation for more details on this section. encryption.className=com.plateausystems.elms.util.helper.ElmsJceEncryption # The encryption provider. The default is Sun JCE, but any JCE provider can be used. encryption.provider=SunJCE # The encryption algorithm used to encrypt data. The default is Triple-DES (a.k.a. DESede), although any secret # key encryption provider supported by JCE is supported here (DESede, AES, Blowfish, etc). # DES is not to be used as it is consider to be weak. encryption.algorithm=DESede # As of TMS 6.2.3, the encryption key is now a wrapped key value (so the value of encryption.key below may look # like it is a new value but actually it just represents a wrapped version of the original encryption key). # If you have never changed the value of the encryption.key setting, and you are upgrading to 6.2.3 or later, # use the encryption.key value provided here (rather than the old key which ended in \"==\"). # For extra security, a new random key value can be obtained with the JceEncryption command-line utility. # For even extra security, you can install the JCE Unlimited Strength Jurisdiction Policy Files 6 and use keys larger than 128-bit. encryption.key=***** encryption.mode= encryption.padding= # **** System Settings: Database Preferences **** # Do NOT change database preferences after initial set up of your system. # Java date and time pattern. Use Java Simple Date format dbPreferencesDatePattern.pattern=MM/dd/yyyy dbPreferencesTimePattern.pattern=hh:mm:ss aaa dbPreferencesLanguageCode=en dbPreferencesCountryCode=US # SQL date and time pattern used to form the SQL for the particular database; # needs to match with the above patterns. Use Oracle Datetime format syntax. dbDatePattern=mm/dd/yyyy dbTimePattern=hh:mi:ss AM #  This is maximum year value for a date. This value depends on the deployed database. Default: 9999 maxDbSupportedYear=9999 # **** System Settings: Validation Settings **** # Defines limits to the size (positive and negative) of numbers, by type. # Properties minValue and maxValue hold the min and the max for numbers of their type (minLongValue is for Long type, for example) # Long default: min: -9999999999  max: 9999999999 minLongValue=-9999999999 maxLongValue=9999999999 # Double default: min: -9999999999.00 max: 9999999999.00 minDoubleValue=-9999999999.00 maxDoubleValue=9999999999.00 # **** System Settings: Caching **** # Inserts scripts to control the caching of pages by the browser. The property proxyCaching controls caching for Microsoft Internet Explorer. # The property nsBrowserCaching controls the caching for Mozilla browsers. By default, both are set to false. proxyCaching=false nsBrowserCaching=false # **** System Settings: Web Services **** # Set the webServicesenabled property to true if you want the Web Services to be accessible. Default: false. # Web Services are also enabled if successfactorsLearningEnabled is also set to true in SuccessFactorsLearningConfiguration even if the setting here is false webServicesEnabled=false # **************************************** # ******** I18N BEHAVIOR SETTINGS ******** # **************************************** # These settings configure the behavior of the application when a label is requested but is not found in the locale label cache. # If logging is desired, isI18nLabelExceptionLoggingEnabled should be enabled (set to true) and the log4j configuration file can be tweaked as desired # (defaults to a separate missinglabels.log file in the logs folder).  If desired, a stack trace can also be spit out for missing # label detection up to a depth specified in the stackTraceDepthForMissingLabelLogging.  If this attribute is missing or zero, no # stack trace will be output with the error message logged for the missing label. isI18nLabelExceptionLoggingEnabled=false stackTraceDepthForMissingLabelLogging=7 #This configuration is used to show/hide the locale selector for an unauthenticated user in the system default header when more than one active locale exists. showPreferenceSelectorInDefaultHeader=false #This is only for V1 label cache # Once a label has been determined not to be in the cached label set, the default behavior of the application is to check the DB # again to see if the label was added since the last label cache read.  This can be turned OFF by setting the enabled attribute # of the allowRepeatedDBLookups property to false.  Otherwise, the i18nMissingLabelStatusTTL attribute is the number of milliseconds to # wait for any given label between DB lookups.  This can improve performance at the cost of a temporarily stale missing label # by preventing too many DB lookups for the same missing label.  If zero, there is no delay - all missing label lookups # go to the DB each time.  This would be useful in a development phase of the application.  However, for production it is recommended # to give this value an acceptable time to wait for labels to be loaded.  Default recommendation is 10 minutes (600,000 milliseconds). allowRepeatedDBLookups=true i18nMissingLabelStatusTTL=600000 #This is only for V1 label cache # If all labels added post-production begin with a known set of prefixes, use this section to configure those known prefixes # so that the DB lookup processing for missing labels is fine-tuned to apply to only labels matching these \"starts-with\" # patterns.  For each bracketed value, the value of the element becomes a case-sensitive pattern # matched against a missing label ID.  If the label ID starts with any of the patterns listed here, it is eligible for another # DB lookup after the i18nMissingLabelStatusTTL has elapsed. allowRepeatedDBLookupsForLabelsStartingWith[label.u.]=true # ************************************** # ******** HELP SYSTEM SETTINGS ******** # ************************************** # Configure baseHelpRedirectURL to point to the location where the help.war file is deployed. # By default this is a WAR file inside of the TMS package (webapps folder), so the context path is simply /help. # If deployed outside the EAR, you should give a complete URL, e.g. http://www.plateau.com/TMSHelp # The helpRedirectorURI is the URI (/contextPath/redirectorURI?params...) that will be used for initial help links. # Change the helpRedirectorURI only if you change the struts action or want to go through a custom redirector baseHelpRedirectURL=/help helpRedirectorURI=/getHelpRedirector.do # ******************************************** # ******** LEARNING CONTENT SETTINGS ********* # ******************************************** # # **** Learning Content Settings: Content **** # # Servlet mapping for the PwsAiccServlet, external AICC courseware will send HTTP message to this URL # PwsAicc Servlet tracks the completion of external AICC content through HTTP messages. aiccReturnURL=/PwsAicc # Window options when launching different course types. contentWindowOpenOptions.aicc=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1 contentWindowOpenOptions.scorm=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1 contentWindowOpenOptions.browser=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1 contentWindowOpenOptions.document=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1 # When content is opened inline in the same browser window, the size of the IFrame that # contains the content is controlled by these settings. You can set different sizes for each # launch method that supports opening a content object inline. The configuration is specified # as an integer percentage value (20-100) of the parent browser window size. # If a value is not specified it will default to 80 inlineContentWindowSize.aicc.width=80 inlineContentWindowSize.aicc.height=80 inlineContentWindowSize.scorm.width=80 inlineContentWindowSize.scorm.height=80 inlineContentWindowSize.browser.width=80 inlineContentWindowSize.browser.height=80 # Servlet mapping for the PwsTrackingFuncitonsServlet, the tracking applet will send HTTP message to this URL # PwsTrackingFunction Servlet tracks the completion of Plateau Structured content. Default: /PwsTrackingFunction contentTrackingFunctionReturnURL=/PwsTrackingFunction # Servlet mapping for the SCORM 2004 RTE Servlet, the PlateauSCORM2004API applet will send HTTP message to this URL # SCORM 2004 RTE tracks the completion of SCORM 2004 content. Default: /ScormRteServlet scorm2004ReturnURL=/ScormRteServlet # Servlet mapping for the PwsStudentExamApi, the Exam Question will send HTTP message to this URL. # PwsStudentExamApi tracks exam completion. Default: /PwsStudentExamApi examQuestionReturnURL=/PwsStudentExamApi # The Online Content Structure page expires after being idle for this amount of time (in seconds) # The expired page transitions to a page that supports content communication (AICC and SCORM). #   When the user returns to the Online Content Structure page it is updated with content statuses. Default: 120 contentStructurePageExpireDuration=120 # The Online Content Structure page has a LMSsession keep alive feature that is based on this amount of time (in seconds). # Default: 300 (5 min) # 0 - Session timeout-600 (i.e. 10 minutes based on the 30 min session time out);  Minimum : 120 (i.e. 2 minutes) contentStructurePageKeepAliveInterval=300 # This is an opt in setting to extend the User session to 4 hours while taking the AICC content. # It will reset back to normal however when user navigates back to the home page, i.e. away from the content launching page. extendAiccOnlineSession=false # The maximum number of resources that will be cached by the PexamResorceServlet. Default: 100 examResourceCacheMaxCount=100 # **** Learning Content Settings: Learning Component Settings **** # # The Vle element enables connection between Plateau and Virtual Learning Servers (VLS) such as WebEx. # When you set vleEnabled to true, you must also configure the VLS. See VLS Configuration Guide. # Setting Vle to true shows the VLS tabs in the administration environment. Default: false vleEnabled=false # When adHocEmailTemplateUsageEnabled is set to true, users can select a template in the Ad Hoc Notifications wizard. # When set to false, they cannot select a template. # This element only applies in an OnDemand license - Product license environments ignore it. Default: true. adHocEmailTemplateUsageEnabled=true # **** Learning Content Settings: Security Settings **** # # Enforce security on AICC content. For example, security does not allow # users to copy URLs to take over other user's AICC sessions. By default, set to false. # Note: since b1311 this flag is deprecated and no longer being used. Security has to be turned on for all AICC communications. aiccSecurityEnabled=true # Access-Control-Allow-Origin CORS header for the AICC endpoint PwsAicc # Enable it to allow AICC content hosted on a different domain (cross-domain content) to communicate with LMS server via Ajax, i.e XMLHttpRequest aiccAccessControlAllowOriginEnabled=false #specify your content server domain instead of * for better security, such as https://developer.mozilla.org aiccAccessControlAllowOriginHeader=* # Sets debugging pages for online support contentTestPagesEnabled=false # Enabling this setting stores the current User ID, name in the cookie. This information may be required for certain third party content # to work properly. Customers can enable this setting in that case. userIdentityInformationCookieEnabled=false # **** Learning Content Settings: Cross Domain Support Settings **** # # Cookie Cross domain support is used to support launching and tracking courseware from a different domain than the TMS domain. # TMS and the content server must however share the top level domain for cross domain tracking to be successful. # The value of cookieCrossDomainSupportDomainName is the top level domain. Thus an LMS with domain lms.plateausystems.com and a content server # with domain cms.plateausystems.com share the top level domain plateausystems.com. # Default of cookieCrossDomainSupportEnabled: false cookieCrossDomainSupportEnabled=false cookieCrossDomainSupportDomainName=plateausystems.com # Communication Cross domain support is used to support launching and tracking courseware from a different domain than the LMS. communicationCrossDomainSupportEnabled=false # The DefaultContentServerPath specifies the URI path where the TMS support files required by content reside on the content server. # Absolute URL can be specified, or else a URI path that is relative to the TMS base URL (must start with a slash). defaultContentServerPath=http://contentserver:7000/content contentWrapperPageName=main_content_wrapper.html scorm2004ContentWrapperPageName=scorm_2004_content_wrapper.html externalURLQuestionWrapperPageName=main_question_wrapper.html contentOpenerPageName=main_content_opener.html # The defaultProxletPath specifies the URI Path to Cross Domain Proxlet. This path does not include the Servlet mapping. # Absolute URL can be specified, or else a URI path that is relative to the TMS base URL (must start with a slash). defaultProxletPath=http://contentserver:7000/proxlet lmsSessionId=JSESSIONID #When set to true, item content structure is locked for any item that has at least one associated history record. Content cannot be added to, removed from or moved within a locked content structure. To enable editing of the content structure set to false. # WARNING: changes to the content structure could result in inability to review from history or inability to complete the course if not reassigned. lockItemContentStructure=false # ***************************************** # ******** BACKGROUND JOB SETTINGS ******** # ***************************************** ### **** Background Job Windows ***** # Background jobs are asynchronous jobs that an administrator can set up and pass to the Scheduler.  Background jobs can be scheduled # only during allowable time frames, described below with the allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes settings. Each allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes # element defines a window: a date and time during which administrators can run a background job. Make them times that the system is under light loads. # By default, each day is contained in brackets. '...[Monday].enabled' means that background jobs will run on Mondays. # However, the bracketed text is just a string to denote one window. You could also, for example create a [Weekdays] and [Weekends] window. # The default below one example of a non-day bracketed value, [Christmas]. # For each bracketed day, you can define start and end minutes, hours, dates, months, etc. A * means any of the unit. so if you have a * in minutes # and start/end hours between 0 and 5, then jobs can start on any minute between the hours of Midnight and 5 AM. # Note that hours are in 24-hour format so that 0 is Midnight and 13 is 1 PM. allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startDayofWeek=mon allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endDayofWeek=mon allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startDayofWeek=tue allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endDayofWeek=tue allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startDayofWeek=wed allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endDayofWeek=wed allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startDayofWeek=thu allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endDayofWeek=thu allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startDayofWeek=fri allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endDayofWeek=fri allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startDayofWeek=sat allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endDayofWeek=sat allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startDayofWeek=sun allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endDayofWeek=sun allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startDate=25 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startMonth=12 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startDayofWeek=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endDate=25 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endMonth=12 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endDayofWeek=*  allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].startMinute=0 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].startHour=0 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].startDayofWeek=sat allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].endMinute=59 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].endHour=23 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].endDayofWeek=sat allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].startMinute=0 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].startHour=0 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].startDayofWeek=sun allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].endMinute=59 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].endHour=11 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].endDayofWeek=sun  ### **** Limits and Timing in Background Jobs **** # lateTimeWindow sets a time expression (in minutes) that indicates the latest a timer trigger may fire past its scheduled firing time without being skipped. # For example, a late time window of \"30\" means that a job may fire up to thirty minutes late.  If the job is more than thirty minutes late, that job firing # is skipped. lateTimeWindow=30 # enableMakupFiring allows the last late firing to occur. For example, suppose a job is scheduled to fire once a day, the scheduler is down for a day, and the # late time window is small enough such that all these firings would be skipped when the engine begins running again. If makeup firings are not enabled, then # these late jobs will not fire. On the other hand, if makeup firings are enabled, then the last late job will fire. enableMakeupFiring=true # useItemLibraryBackgroundJob allows using background job for adding items to catalog. useItemLibraryBackgroundJob=false # Specifies the maximum number of e-mail messages that will be purged from mail archive at any one time. Default: 10000 emailArchivePurgeBatchCount=1000 # Specifying the batch size greater than 0 (zero) enables the processing of the records in batches. # This gives the ability to the user to commit the transaction after each batch has been processed. Default: 1000 numberOfRecordsToBeProcessedInABatch=1000 # Configuration for specific background/APM jobs.  Use Constants defined in the ApmConstants class for the background job names. # The job will be committed for every batch (transactionCommitSize), temporarily pausing for a number (sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches) of milliseconds # between jobs. apmJobSettings.TRNGEXPIRE.enabled=true apmJobSettings.TRNGEXPIRE.sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches=99 apmJobSettings.TRNGEXPIRE.transactionCommitSize=10000 apmJobSettings.EXTERNALREQUESTFORMDATAUPGRADER.enabled=true apmJobSettings.EXTERNALREQUESTFORMDATAUPGRADER.transactionCommitSize=500 apmJobSettings.ITEMJAMGROUPSNOTIFICATION.enabled=true apmJobSettings.ITEMJAMGROUPSNOTIFICATION.sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches=99 apmJobSettings.ITEMJAMGROUPSNOTIFICATION.transactionCommitSize=10000 apmJobSettings.USERHISTORYPURGE.enabled=true apmJobSettings.USERHISTORYPURGE.sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches=99 apmJobSettings.USERHISTORYPURGE.transactionCommitSize=100 # If the number of records that an operation operates on exceeds this count, the operation may have to be scheduled as a background job to run later instead of running online. # It is not recommended to choose a value greater than 100. # Assignment Profile jobs are also affected by the Assignment Profile Job specific settings below. onlineOperationMaxRecordsCount=5 # Defines the batch size for learning event resync commits.  0 - no limit. Default: 50. learningEventResynchronizationStudentCommitCount=50 # ### **** Settings Specific to the Assignment Profile Propagation and Synchronization Job **** # # The queries are batched and executed at one time. This setting determines how many queries are executed in one batch. Default: 1000 assignmentProfileBatchSize=1000 # Determines if operator data is read once and cached in memory or is re-read from the database during each background job. Default: true assignmentProfileMetaDataCache=true # Class implementing the AssignmentProfileQueryHelper interface used to generate query strings that determine which users should be # associated with an assignment profile.  Default: com.plateausystems.elms.bo.assignmentprofile.helper.AssignmentProfileQueryHelperImpl assignmentProfileQueryHelper=com.plateausystems.elms.bo.assignmentprofile.helper.AssignmentProfileQueryHelperImpl # The maximum number of records committed during any one transaction. Default: 100 assignmentProfileTxnCommitBatchSize=100 # ********************************************************* # ****** ALL USERS/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS ******* # ********************************************************* # These settings affect both the Admin and End User interaction. # **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Upload Limits **** # # fileUploadMaxSize is the maximum size in bytes for files uploaded to the server. It can be between 0 and 2147483647(2 GB). Default 10485760 bytes (10Mb) fileUploadMaxSize=10485760 # fileUploadFilenameMaxSize is the maximum amount of characters for a file name to be uploaded to the server. Default: 255 fileUploadFilenameMaxSize=255 # Settings specific to PQE, which is a module of Talent Management. # resourceUploadMaxSize is the limit, in bytes, of any image file uploaded to the server through PQE. # Question authors can change the \"size\" of an image file, but they are not changing the actual size in the database. # Rather, they are constraining the rendering size. Default: 524288. resourceUploadMaxSize=524288 # resourceUploadWarningSize is the limit, in bytes, of images that are uploaded to PQE without warning. # If the image size is over resourceUploadWarningSize, but below resourceUploadMaxSize, the question author is warned, # but not prevented from uploading the file.  Default: 262144 resourceUploadWarningSize=262144 # **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Privacy **** # # If hideUserPhotosGlobally is set to true all employee photos will be hidden EVERYWHERE in the application (admin and end user interfaces). Default: true hideUserPhotosGlobally=true # PrivacyAct Masks enable the student ID and/or the instructor ID to be hidden when a notification is sent # or when a report is printed. # Default mask. Admin running the report can change it at report time. Default: ********* privacyActDefaultMask=********* # Masks can be applied to notifications # Attribute module is the name of the module. When attribute enabled set to true, fields are masked in the module # By default, two modules are enabled: \"notification\" and \"report.\" privacyActMaskEnabled.Notification.StudentID=true privacyActMaskEnabled.Notification.InstructorID=true privacyActMaskEnabled.Report.StudentID=true privacyActMaskEnabled.Report.InstructorID=true # **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Error Checking and Reporting **** # # Set to true to show the stack trace to the user in browser (recommended for development and test environments). # Set to false (default setting) to only report ticket number to user in the browser (recommended for production environments). # Whether set to true or false, errors are always logged through Log4J with a ticket number (by default in the plateau.log file). reportStackTraceToUser=false # When emailValidationEnabled is set to true, the class in emailValidationClassName is called to validate e-mail syntax. # When a user types in an e-mail address, the system checks for @ symbols and periods (.) for correct e-mail syntax. Default: true. emailValidationEnabled=true # See JavaDoc for details about syntax checking in EmailValidationImpl # Default:com.plateausystems.elms.util.helper.EmailValidationImpl emailValidationClassName=com.plateausystems.elms.util.helper.EmailValidationImpl # **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Legacy Reports **** # # Set to true to show the legacy reports (reports defined with old report framework) in the report menus (both admin and end users). # Default: false showLegacyReports=false # ******************************************************************* # ******** END USER/APPLICATION INTERACTION BEHAVIOR **************** # ******************************************************************* ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Exam Settings *** # # Global setting whether to freeze the other component objects while the exam is in progress. # Default setting is true.  Set to false to allow \"open book\" tests. restrictAccessToOtherComponentObjectsDuringExam=true # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Learning Plan Configuration *** # # Set to true to show the Days Remaining Column rather than the Required by column in the Learning Plan Page and the Curriculum Details page. Default: false showDaysRemaining=false # Set to true to show the Assignment Type Column in the Learning Plan Page, the Curriculum Details page, and in the Home page. Default: false. showAssignmentType=false # learningPlanFieldsChooserItems controls the columns that users can enable and disable on the learning plan and some properties of the column. # The settings have attributes that identify the column, control the user interaction, call the column title, and control the width. # The attributes are: visibility - controls if user is forced to show column (mandatory), if column shows by default (default) # or if the column can be turned on or off by the user (optional) / titleLabelID - the label (from the I18N settings in the admin environment) # that appears at the top of the column / width - the default width of the column. learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.columnID=title learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.titleLabelID=label.Title learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.visibility=mandatory learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.width=50 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.columnID=itemID learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.titleLabelID=label.ID learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.visibility=optional learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.width=4 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.columnID=itemType learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.titleLabelID=label.Type learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.visibility=default learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.width=4 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.columnID=requiredBy learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.titleLabelID=label.RequiredBy learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.visibility=default learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.width=4 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.columnID=status learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.titleLabelID=label.Status learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.visibility=default learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.width=8 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.columnID=daysRemaining learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.titleLabelID=label.DaysRemaining learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.visibility=optional learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.width=4 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.columnID=assignmentType learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.titleLabelID=label.AssignmentType learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.visibility=optional learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.width=8 # The system default user learning plan settings. User can override with their own preferences # Defaults the Group By drop-down. Possible values: None, ItemType, AssignmentType,DueWithin, StatusTowardCompletion. Default: None learningPlanSystemPreferences.groupPlanFilter=None # Defaults the Filter By drop-down. Possible values: All, With Online Content, Registered, In progress Default: All learningPlanSystemPreferences.itemsFilter=All #  Defaults the Required By drop-down. Possible values: All, Next 30 Days, Next 60 Days, Next 90 Days. Default: All learningPlanSystemPreferences.requiredByFilter=All # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Home Page Settings *** # # Home Page Configuration to indicate which modules are displayed on the home page for users showHomeCatalogModule=true showHomeAlertsModule=true showHomeLearningPlanModule=true showHomeCareerPlanModule=true showHomeCurriculumModule=true showHomeNewItemModule=true showHomeFeaturedItemModule=true showHomeRevisedItemModule=true homeLearningPlanModuleRecordsToDisplay=5 homeCareerPlanModuleRecordsToDisplay=5 homeCurriculumModuleRecordsToDisplay=5 #homeFlaggedCatalogItemsToDisplay specifies the maximum number of flagged items and programs to display for EACH category (e.g. max 25 New, max 25 Revised, and max 25 Featured) homeFlaggedCatalogItemsToDisplay=25 # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Catalog Settings *** # # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Competency Search Settings *** # #This configuration is used for controlling whether on the competency search screen, users by default see all courses they have access to that are tied to the specified competencies, or #just the courses that match or exceed their current competency rating. #False: Users first see just the courses that match or exceed their current competency rating. View only items that help me close competency gaps is enabled by default on the competency search screen. #True: Users first see all courses they have access to that are tied to the specified competencies.View only items that help me close competency gaps is disabled by default on the competency search screen. showAllCoursesByDefault=false # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Calendar Settings *** # # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Persistence/Preferences *** # # Specify if the persistence can be lazy (does not have to happen immediately) and what class manages it. Default: true studentSubordinatesLazyPersistence=true studentSubordinatesPreferencesHandler=com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.StudentSubordinatesUIPreferencesHandler # The handler class that persists UI state preferences related to the user. # Default: com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.StudentUIPreferencesHandler studentUIPreferencesHandler=com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.StudentUIPreferencesHandler # When set to true the Show Pictures checkbox on the Dashboard / Succession Planner is selected by default. # If hideUserPhotosGlobally is set to true, then ShowPictures is irrelevant. Default: true studentSubordinatesShowPictures=true # When set to true the Show Status checkbox on Dashboard / Succession Planner is selected by default. Default: true studentSubordinatesShowStatus=true # ### ***** End User Interaction Behavior: Icon Preference *** # # Controls the icon preference on the end user interface. Default: true enableFontIcons=true # ### ***** End User Interaction Behavior: Miscellaneous *** # # This setting determines if the competency type is displayed to the user when competencies are displayed. showCompetencyType=true # talent search: max number of students per group talentPoolMaxGroupSize=1000 # This setting indicates the number of days from the current date to search for a new posts in the communities the user has access to. # This setting is used on the user's home page in the Communities button. Valid values are zero and any value greater than zero. searchNewPostsToCommunitiesInTheLastDays=14 # This setting would turn on or off the display of revision date time and number for items on the User's To-Do List. displayRevisionInformationInToDoList=false # This value is the number of reporting levels down displayed to a user and # should be an integer equal to or greater than 0. # Default: 0 # Example: #   If set to 0, the user will see all direct and indirect subordinates. #   If set to 1, the user will see their direct reports only. #   If set to 2, the user will see their direct reports and direct reports reporting into their direct reports and so on reportingLevelsToDisplay=0 # This configuration controls the display of the News page upon Login. Valid values are below (Values are case-sensitive): # Never : News page would not display on login. user would still have the ability to get to news page from the Easy link menu # Always : News page would always display on user login. User cannot dismiss this # UserDiscretion : News page would display upon login and the user would have the ability to not display each time. This is the default value displayNewsPageOnLogin=UserDiscretion # ********************************************************** # ******** ADMIN/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS ********** # ********************************************************** # ### **** Admin Application UI Behavior Configuration: Sticky Preferences **** # # Specify if the persistence can be lazy (does not have to happen immediately). Default: true userUILazyPersistence=true # This section is used for setting the handler class that will persist UI state preferences related to Tab Modes. # Default: com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.UserUIPreferencesHandler userUIPreferencesHandler=com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.UserUIPreferencesHandler # Defaults the administrator's view of users' learning plans. Administrator can set own preference. If the option is true # then, by default, dates are displayed in the User's preferred time zone. If false, it is displayed in the Admin's preferred time zone. Default: true learningPlanDisplayInLearnerTimezone=true # ### **** Admin Application UI Behavior Configuration: Limits **** # # The maximum rating an administrator is allowed to give a learning item. # Admins assign ratings on the Item Summary tab and can appear to end users in catalog. # Whether or not ratings appear in the catalog is controlled by the showItemRatingInCatalog property (CatalogConfiguration). maxItemRatingValue=5.0 # Limits the amount of copies that the Copy Scheduled Offering Wizard can make in the Admin Environment. # Limit applies to the amount of copies the admin can make any ONE time they run the wizard. # Setting a reasonable limit prevents admins from mistakenly overwhelming database. Default: 50 scheduleCopiesLimit=50 # Limits the amount of \"recents\" entries that can be seen on the Admin Recents Panel # Setting a reasonable limit prevents admins from overwhelming database. # Default Value\t: 50 / Min Value: 1 / Max Value: 100 maxNumberOfRecentsDisplayed=50 # ### **** Admin Application UI Behavior Configuration: Security/Self Modification *** # When restrictUserSelfModification is set to \"true\" administrators cannot change their own records. # For example, when set to true, an administrator \"jdoe\" with permissions to change administrator accounts, # can change all other administrator password and permissions *except* for his own. # Default value is true. We recommend true. Possible values are true or false. You might set to # false in development or training environments, for convenience. restrictUserSelfModification=true # ### **** User E-Signature PIN Self Reset Configuration *** # This configuration determines whether learners can reset their E-Signature PIN if they forget it. # By default, the property is set to true. When true, learners can use \"Forgot My PIN\" on the \"Options and Settings\" page to receive a secure email link, allowing them to create a new PIN. # When set to false, the \"Forgot My PIN\" option is hidden. enableESignatureResetPIN=true # This flag is used to order module tabs alphabetically. By default, it is true and module tabs will be displayed in alphabetical order # except for the Summary tab. Setting it to false will result in module tabs being ordered as they historically have been before this # configuration was introduced. displayModuleTabsInAlphabeticalOrder=true #This flag is used to enable the new supervisor enhancements for Assign/Remove learning, Record learning and Register/Witdraw Users. #The Old supervisor flow is deprecated. #Configuration options: true is the only valid option updatedSupervisorFlow=true #The maximum number of Users a Supervisor can register or withdraw using the Register / Withdraw Employees Wizard. The minimum value can be 1 and the maximum can be 1000. supervisorMaxUserRegisterWithdrawLimit=50 #This flag is used to enable the new tool for user Record learning. #The Old Self Record Learning flow is deprecated. #Configuration options: true is the only valid option updatedSelfRecordLearningFlow=true # ************************************************************************************************** # WARNING: No Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) filtering will be done if the URL is specified here as \"true\". # It is strongly recommended that you consult Plateau before modifying these values. xssFilterExcludedURLs[/globalErrorDispatcher.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editAppAdminStudent.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateAppAdminStudent.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateConfiguration.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editConfigurationSummary.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateSearchSelector.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editSearchSelector.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateUIDataSummary.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editUIDataSummary.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/addUIDataSummary.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/showSystemConfigurationReport.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/editPrintedExamTemplate.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/updatePrintedExamTemplate.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/getSecurityQuestion.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/references/updateOrg.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/references/editOrg.do]=true # XSS filtering for Notification Template messages can be turned on/off using the WEB_SECURITY configuration setting enableXSSFiltersForNotificationTemplateMessages. # The settings in this block control whether XSS filtering is applied to URLs related to Notification Template messages. # When these URLs are excluded from XSS filtering (=true), Notification Template messages will allow inclusion of IMG tags and special characters. # When these URLs are included in XSS filtering (=false), inclusion of IMG tags and special characters is disallowed. xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/previewNotificationTemplateMessages.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateNotificationTemplateMessages.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editNotificationTemplateMessages.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/listLabelNotificationTemplate.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/addNotificationTemplateMessage.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/sendNotificationAssistantStep5.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/student/previewCertificateOfCompletion.do]=true # Enable to allow admin update locale labels with such as <li> html tags, when for instance the # secRules.specialCharsNotAllowed.enabled XSS filter is turned on. #xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/updateI18nActiveLocaleLabel.do]=true #request URL endings which can qualify the requests to be scanned xssFilterURLSuffix[.jsp]=true # These URLs which are outside of the regular *.jsp and *.do also need to be scanned xssFilterAdditionalURLs[/admin_acegi_authenticate]=true xssFilterAdditionalURLs[/student_acegi_authenticate]=true xssFilterAdditionalURLs[/site_acegi_authenticate]=true # Sets the login page behaviour to-remember or not-to-remember login crendentials. # Possible values are true/false. autoCompleteLoginForUser=true autoCompleteLoginForAdmin=true # This configuration is used to enable the online content early launch warning. This configuration # is added in b1207 # true: will enable the early launch warning. # false: will disable the early launch warning. enableOnlineContentEarlyLaunchWarning=true #This configuration specifies the threshold for online content launch warning and is only #applicable when the \"enableOnlineContentEarlyLaunchWarning\" is set to true. # The value is number of days and should be a positive integer greater than or equal to 0. onlineContentEarlyLaunchWarningThreshold=45 # ************************************************************************************************** # Opted in Features Related Settings # ************************************************************************************************** # This configuration is used to determine whether to use default password functionality or new initial random password generation. Added in b1207 # true: will enable random password generation for all the users created in our system. # false: will use default password functionality. enableRandomPasswordGenerationForNewUsers=false # This configuration is used to enable item and program recommendations feature. This is added in b1207 # true: will enable item and program recommedations feature. # false: will disable item and program recommendations feature. enableItemRecommendations=true # This configuration enforces the security domain restrictions set for the Edit Class permission when marking class attendance. The default value is false. # When set to true, any security domain restrictions for the Edit Class permission apply to marking class attendance. Only administrators with the necessary security domain permissions can mark attendance for classes. # When set to false, the security domain restrictions for the Edit Class permission don't apply to marking class attendance. Administrators with the Edit Class permission can mark attendance for classes, regardless of the configured security domain permissions. enforceSecurityDomainRestrictionForMarkingAttendance=false # ************************************************************************************************** # Peer Recommendation settings # ************************************************************************************************** # The Peer Recommendation would be hidden after the user has viewed the recommendation by navigating # to the Item / Program details page from the Recommendation tile and the entity has been added # to the Learning Plan or is part of the Learning History. This is to make the behavior # consistent with the Admin recommendations # This setting is deprecated and no longer used as of the 2H 2023 release. hideViewedP2PRecommendations=true # This configuration is the number of days after which a Peer Recommendation is deleted from the system. # After the number of configured days, a peer recommendation that has not been removed by the recipient will no longer appear in the peer recommendation section of the application. # The default value is 365 days. You can enter a value for this property only between 30 and 730 days. Revise the value to continue. peerRecommendationExpiration=365 # This configuration is used to choose the type of links to be included in the notification email. This is a system level configuration that is to be chosen based on the level of authentication needed. This is added in b1505 # true: will enable SmartLinks with personalized tokens for users to provide access without a login. # false: will provide a directlink to the recommended external link that requires a login to authenticate the user. enableSmartLinks=true # This configuration is used to enable multiple security questions for a user. This is added in b1210 enableMultipleSecurityQuestionsForUser=false # This configuration will enable or disable offline login page. offlinePlayerLoginRequired=true # This configuration controls whether Offline Player can be upgraded by users. # Warning: If this configuration is set to false, users will not be able to download the Offline Player from Options and Settings. offlinePlayerUpgradeEnabled=true #Local offline url for communications offlinePlayerLocalUrl=http://localhost:53759/learningoffline # If showItemThumbnailPhotosGlobally is set to false, the Thumbnail File and Thumbnail URL fields will be hidden from the admin interface for Item and Program records. If set to true, the thumbnail fields are displayed on the admin interface which allows an admin to override the system default for a specific Item or Program; Item also requires the fields to be displayed on the record configuration. Default: false showItemThumbnailPhotosGlobally=true # This configuration is used to determine maximum number of seats a supervisor can reserve while adding/editing a training requesting. Default: 500 # Setting a reasonable limit prevents admins from overwhelming database. # Default Value\t: 500 / Min Value: 1 / Max Value: 10000 maxNumberOfTrainingRequestSeats=100 # This configuration enables automatic assignment of training requests if the organization has been reviewed and either the seats requested equals seats granted # or the preselected user count is equal or less than the seats granted. Default: false. Possible values true/false autoAssignReviewedTrainingRequests=false # This configuration is used during the auto assignments of training requests, if the default assignment type is not provided for the items defaultAssignmentTypeForAutoAssignTrainingRequests= # showSystemDefaultThumbnail decides whether the default thumbnail style is a photo (true) or an icon (false). Note that the system default thumbnail can be overridden for most learning at System Admin>Configuration>Images. showSystemDefaultThumbnail=true # This configuration is used to enable HTML descriptions. Default: false enableHTMLDescriptions=true # Setting the allowFutureHireDates property to true enables the creation/update of user records with a future hire date. Default: false # Setting it back to false prevents the creation/update of user records with a future hire date but does not perform any data cleanup on existing records. allowFutureHireDates=false # Setting the enableCappingFactor to true enables Capping Factor feature.This will make the learning event recorder to display system default currency instead of the drop-down.It wont allow to change the currency for addition costs in Learning Event Editor. This will also hide Training days while recording learning. Default: false enableCappingFactor=false # This configuration is used to enable/disable the notification header and footer support. enableNotificationHeaderFooter=false # This configuration is used to set the maximum number of days that an admin is able to download their export # file results in the data export tool.  After the number of configured days, the admin will no longer be able # to access the export results. The allowable range is between 1-30 days.  Recommended default setting is 3. exportExpiration=3 # This flag is used to allow if admins can enter/modify data in the registration form custom columns when registering/modifying users enrollment allowAdminToModifyRegistrationFormCustomColumns=true allowSupervisorToEnterRegistrationFormCustomColumnsData=true allowUserToModifyCustomColumnsDataIfRegisteredBySuper=false allowUserToModifyCustomColumnsDataIfRegisteredByAdmin=false # This configuration specifies the maximum number of subordinates displayed under any node, including the top-level nodes when displaying employees in the \"My Team\" tree-view maxNumberOfSubordinatesDisplayedInTree=300 # The following configuration allows the admin to identify whether or not users can submit incomplete surveys for surveys that are set as \"optional\". This setting applies to # both Item Evaluation and Follow-up Evaluation survey types UsersCanSubmitIncompleteOptionalSurveys=false #Enables the Manage Learning Tool from a scheduled offering. manageLearningToolEnabled=false # This configuration allows the publishing of events to the Service Event Bus (SEB) to be enabled or disabled, based on the SEB-supported event type. #If the destination is unavailable at the time the event is published to the SEB, the event publication fails. You can enable rerunFailedSebPublishedEvents to process the failed events from previous days. You can rerun events for up to 30 days prior to the current day. The number of prior days to reprocess is set in numberOfPriorDaysToRerunSebPublishedEvents. sebPublishedEventTypes[LearningCompletion]=false rerunFailedSebPublishedEvents=false numberOfPriorDaysToRerunSebPublishedEvents=1 # When set to true, if a self-registering user provides an email address, the system will not register the user unless that email address is unique across all users of the system selfRegistrationUniqueEmailAddressRequired=false # This configuration can be used to indicate whether the LMS instance is integrated with Jam or not. # (Note: this property replaces the previously used 'enableSocialTabInCatalogSearch' property.) # true: Indicates that Jam integration available and enabled # false: Indicates that Jam integration is not available or disabled jamIntegrationEnabled=false #When set to true, the from field of the email notification will be replaced with the the recipient's org email. useOrgEmailAsFromForNotifications=false #This configuration is dependent on Course Home being enabled (enableCourseHomeBlended=true). #When set to true, content will always launch inline, regardless of the content-level setting. #When set to false, the content-level setting determines the launch method. #Default value is false. overrideContentLaunchInNewWindow=false #This configuration will enable the content object Audit #When set to true , new field(enable_content_audit) is visible on item snapshot for online and blended courses #when enable_content_audit is set to true , the content communication is saved to Audit table i.e., PA_CBT_STUD_CPNT_MOD_AUDIT enableContentObjectAuditTrail=false # This property applies to the new Learning experience to show or hide the Required Learning section. The default value is set to false. # If no required courses are assigned to users, and you want to hide the section for them, set the property to true. This property applies to specific organizations and user groups where the section is set to be hidden. #When hideRequiredLearningSectionOnLearningPortal is set to true, users do not see the Required Learning section on their Learning Portal. Note that when there is content on the Required Learning section, setting the property to true does not hide the section on users' Learning Portal. #When hideRequiredLearningSectionOnLearningPortal is set to false, the Required Learning section appears on the users' Learning Portal. hideRequiredLearningSectionOnLearningPortal=false # When this configuration is enabled, the Purge Deleted User Audit # History APM will add a list of the purged users to PA_USER_PURGE_LOG. # Disabling this configuration does not delete any previously added records. # WARNING: Enabling purge logging will prevent reusing a purged User ID in the future. enablePurgeLog=false # This KBA feature depends on the System Setting enableErrorFingerprinting JVM flag. # If the enableErrorFingerprinting flag is false, this setting will be considered as false always. # Set it to false to opt out enableKBASearchService=true # When this configuration is enabled, the user can view the Learning History of all Employments. # Set the learningHistoryOfAllEmployments flag as false to opt out. learningHistoryOfAllEmployments=false # For customers integrated with Talent Intelligence Hub, setting this configuration to true allows users to view the legacy 'Competencies' entity in the menu, in addition to the 'Attributes' entity. # The competency search selector functionality remains the same. showCompetenciesMenuAfterTalentIntelligenceHubMigration=false #This configuration prevents intermittent early completion issues for SCORM 2004 4th edition content that occur when a learner navigates away from or exits content. #When set to true, this configuration assumes that the completionSetByContent and objectiveSetByContent values in the content manifest are true, so Learning records completion only after the content communicates completion. #The default value is false and the setting values in the content manifest determine how content completion is communicated. contentCommunicatesCompletion=true #This configuration allows the continued use of unload browser events for online content and is enabled (true) by default. # This temporary setting is intended to allow customers additional time to replace unload browser events for their online content and will only be available until Google deprecates support in 2025. enableContentUnloadEventUsage=true #This configuration is specific to ILX and decides the behaviour of primary actions related to Launch Course on ILX cards #When set to true, the primary actions related to Launch Course would redirect to Course Home page. #When set to false, the primary actions related to Launch Course would redirect directly to Course Launch. navigateToCourseHomeForILXLaunchCourseActions=false #The configuration determines whether additional details for learning cards, such as learning ID, rating, description, associated skills, and other metadata, are shown in the \"Details\" popover when a learner selects a learning card on the new Learning home page. #The default is set to true, where the \"Details\" popover appears with the additional information for a learning. #When set to false, learners are redirected to the \"Course Home\" page, without displaying the popover. displayAdditionalDetailsForLearningCards=true #The configuration determines whether deleting iContent files using the iContent Management tool also removes the content structure from its linked courses. The default value is set to false. #When set to false, deleting files retains the content structure in all associated courses. You need to manually remove the deleted content from the structure and reactivate the course. #When set to true, deleting files automatically removes the content structure from all associated courses. While the remaining content is still accessible, it is no longer linked to the course. removeContentStructureOnDelete=false #The configuration determines whether learners can access the redesigned \"Program Details\", \"Curriculum Details\" and \"Curricula Status\" pages from the Learning home page. #The default is false where learners continue to access the legacy pages. #Set it to true for learners to access the redesigned pages. enableLegacyUIReplacement=true  # This configuration controls whether the user should be allowed to access course in a program which has approvals. # When set to false (default), users are not restricted from accessing courses in programs with approvals. # When set to true, the system enforces approval requirements for accessing courses in programs. honorApprovalsForPrograms=true  # This configuration controls whether the system honors prerequisites when managing learning programs. # When set to true, the system enforces prerequisite requirements for program enrollment and completion. # When set to false, prerequisite enforcement is disabled, allowing users to access programs without meeting prerequisites. honorPrerequisitesForPrograms=true  Vis konfigurasjonsendringer  Bruk endringer Tilbakestill"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl name=\"Systemkonfigurasjon &#xA0;|&#xA0;Hjelp&#xA0;| &gt; Rediger systemkonfigurasjon Kon*\" role=\"cell\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"name":"Systemkonfigurasjon  | Hjelp | > Rediger systemkonfigurasjon Kon*","role":"cell","aastate":"opaque"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl role=\"row\" idx=\"11\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"role":"row","aastate":"opaque","rowName":"# This configuration contains system administrator information required to configure the Talent Management application. # It is divided into sections to group the concerns: #    SYSTEM: Contains settings for TMS Globally (and not a particular module) #    I18N BEHAVIOR: Contains settings for the internationalization system of Talent Management #    HELP SYSTEM: Contains settings for the help system of Talent Management #    LEARNING CONTENT: Contains settings for the delivery of learning content to users #    BACKGROUND JOB: Contains settings for background job processing #    ALL USERS/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS: Contains settings to control how all users (both admin and end) interact with the application #    END USERS/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS: Contains settings to control how end users interact with the application #    ADMIN/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS: Contains settings to control how administrators interact with the application # **************************************** # *********** SYSTEM SETTINGS ************ # **************************************** # **** System Settings: Encryption Settings **** # The following encryption uses the JavaTM Cryptography Architecture. # Changing any of these values will cause all encrypted data in the database to be re-encrypted using the new settings. # See the documentation for more details on this section. encryption.className=com.plateausystems.elms.util.helper.ElmsJceEncryption # The encryption provider. The default is Sun JCE, but any JCE provider can be used. encryption.provider=SunJCE # The encryption algorithm used to encrypt data. The default is Triple-DES (a.k.a. DESede), although any secret # key encryption provider supported by JCE is supported here (DESede, AES, Blowfish, etc). # DES is not to be used as it is consider to be weak. encryption.algorithm=DESede # As of TMS 6.2.3, the encryption key is now a wrapped key value (so the value of encryption.key below may look # like it is a new value but actually it just represents a wrapped version of the original encryption key). # If you have never changed the value of the encryption.key setting, and you are upgrading to 6.2.3 or later, # use the encryption.key value provided here (rather than the old key which ended in \"==\"). # For extra security, a new random key value can be obtained with the JceEncryption command-line utility. # For even extra security, you can install the JCE Unlimited Strength Jurisdiction Policy Files 6 and use keys larger than 128-bit. encryption.key=***** encryption.mode= encryption.padding= # **** System Settings: Database Preferences **** # Do NOT change database preferences after initial set up of your system. # Java date and time pattern. Use Java Simple Date format dbPreferencesDatePattern.pattern=MM/dd/yyyy dbPreferencesTimePattern.pattern=hh:mm:ss aaa dbPreferencesLanguageCode=en dbPreferencesCountryCode=US # SQL date and time pattern used to form the SQL for the particular database; # needs to match with the above patterns. Use Oracle Datetime format syntax. dbDatePattern=mm/dd/yyyy dbTimePattern=hh:mi:ss AM #  This is maximum year value for a date. This value depends on the deployed database. Default: 9999 maxDbSupportedYear=9999 # **** System Settings: Validation Settings **** # Defines limits to the size (positive and negative) of numbers, by type. # Properties minValue and maxValue hold the min and the max for numbers of their type (minLongValue is for Long type, for example) # Long default: min: -9999999999  max: 9999999999 minLongValue=-9999999999 maxLongValue=9999999999 # Double default: min: -9999999999.00 max: 9999999999.00 minDoubleValue=-9999999999.00 maxDoubleValue=9999999999.00 # **** System Settings: Caching **** # Inserts scripts to control the caching of pages by the browser. The property proxyCaching controls caching for Microsoft Internet Explorer. # The property nsBrowserCaching controls the caching for Mozilla browsers. By default, both are set to false. proxyCaching=false nsBrowserCaching=false # **** System Settings: Web Services **** # Set the webServicesenabled property to true if you want the Web Services to be accessible. Default: false. # Web Services are also enabled if successfactorsLearningEnabled is also set to true in SuccessFactorsLearningConfiguration even if the setting here is false webServicesEnabled=false # **************************************** # ******** I18N BEHAVIOR SETTINGS ******** # **************************************** # These settings configure the behavior of the application when a label is requested but is not found in the locale label cache. # If logging is desired, isI18nLabelExceptionLoggingEnabled should be enabled (set to true) and the log4j configuration file can be tweaked as desired # (defaults to a separate missinglabels.log file in the logs folder).  If desired, a stack trace can also be spit out for missing # label detection up to a depth specified in the stackTraceDepthForMissingLabelLogging.  If this attribute is missing or zero, no # stack trace will be output with the error message logged for the missing label. isI18nLabelExceptionLoggingEnabled=false stackTraceDepthForMissingLabelLogging=7 #This configuration is used to show/hide the locale selector for an unauthenticated user in the system default header when more than one active locale exists. showPreferenceSelectorInDefaultHeader=false #This is only for V1 label cache # Once a label has been determined not to be in the cached label set, the default behavior of the application is to check the DB # again to see if the label was added since the last label cache read.  This can be turned OFF by setting the enabled attribute # of the allowRepeatedDBLookups property to false.  Otherwise, the i18nMissingLabelStatusTTL attribute is the number of milliseconds to # wait for any given label between DB lookups.  This can improve performance at the cost of a temporarily stale missing label # by preventing too many DB lookups for the same missing label.  If zero, there is no delay - all missing label lookups # go to the DB each time.  This would be useful in a development phase of the application.  However, for production it is recommended # to give this value an acceptable time to wait for labels to be loaded.  Default recommendation is 10 minutes (600,000 milliseconds). allowRepeatedDBLookups=true i18nMissingLabelStatusTTL=600000 #This is only for V1 label cache # If all labels added post-production begin with a known set of prefixes, use this section to configure those known prefixes # so that the DB lookup processing for missing labels is fine-tuned to apply to only labels matching these \"starts-with\" # patterns.  For each bracketed value, the value of the element becomes a case-sensitive pattern # matched against a missing label ID.  If the label ID starts with any of the patterns listed here, it is eligible for another # DB lookup after the i18nMissingLabelStatusTTL has elapsed. allowRepeatedDBLookupsForLabelsStartingWith[label.u.]=true # ************************************** # ******** HELP SYSTEM SETTINGS ******** # ************************************** # Configure baseHelpRedirectURL to point to the location where the help.war file is deployed. # By default this is a WAR file inside of the TMS package (webapps folder), so the context path is simply /help. # If deployed outside the EAR, you should give a complete URL, e.g. http://www.plateau.com/TMSHelp # The helpRedirectorURI is the URI (/contextPath/redirectorURI?params...) that will be used for initial help links. # Change the helpRedirectorURI only if you change the struts action or want to go through a custom redirector baseHelpRedirectURL=/help helpRedirectorURI=/getHelpRedirector.do # ******************************************** # ******** LEARNING CONTENT SETTINGS ********* # ******************************************** # # **** Learning Content Settings: Content **** # # Servlet mapping for the PwsAiccServlet, external AICC courseware will send HTTP message to this URL # PwsAicc Servlet tracks the completion of external AICC content through HTTP messages. aiccReturnURL=/PwsAicc # Window options when launching different course types. contentWindowOpenOptions.aicc=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1 contentWindowOpenOptions.scorm=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1 contentWindowOpenOptions.browser=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1 contentWindowOpenOptions.document=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1 # When content is opened inline in the same browser window, the size of the IFrame that # contains the content is controlled by these settings. You can set different sizes for each # launch method that supports opening a content object inline. The configuration is specified # as an integer percentage value (20-100) of the parent browser window size. # If a value is not specified it will default to 80 inlineContentWindowSize.aicc.width=80 inlineContentWindowSize.aicc.height=80 inlineContentWindowSize.scorm.width=80 inlineContentWindowSize.scorm.height=80 inlineContentWindowSize.browser.width=80 inlineContentWindowSize.browser.height=80 # Servlet mapping for the PwsTrackingFuncitonsServlet, the tracking applet will send HTTP message to this URL # PwsTrackingFunction Servlet tracks the completion of Plateau Structured content. Default: /PwsTrackingFunction contentTrackingFunctionReturnURL=/PwsTrackingFunction # Servlet mapping for the SCORM 2004 RTE Servlet, the PlateauSCORM2004API applet will send HTTP message to this URL # SCORM 2004 RTE tracks the completion of SCORM 2004 content. Default: /ScormRteServlet scorm2004ReturnURL=/ScormRteServlet # Servlet mapping for the PwsStudentExamApi, the Exam Question will send HTTP message to this URL. # PwsStudentExamApi tracks exam completion. Default: /PwsStudentExamApi examQuestionReturnURL=/PwsStudentExamApi # The Online Content Structure page expires after being idle for this amount of time (in seconds) # The expired page transitions to a page that supports content communication (AICC and SCORM). #   When the user returns to the Online Content Structure page it is updated with content statuses. Default: 120 contentStructurePageExpireDuration=120 # The Online Content Structure page has a LMSsession keep alive feature that is based on this amount of time (in seconds). # Default: 300 (5 min) # 0 - Session timeout-600 (i.e. 10 minutes based on the 30 min session time out);  Minimum : 120 (i.e. 2 minutes) contentStructurePageKeepAliveInterval=300 # This is an opt in setting to extend the User session to 4 hours while taking the AICC content. # It will reset back to normal however when user navigates back to the home page, i.e. away from the content launching page. extendAiccOnlineSession=false # The maximum number of resources that will be cached by the PexamResorceServlet. Default: 100 examResourceCacheMaxCount=100 # **** Learning Content Settings: Learning Component Settings **** # # The Vle element enables connection between Plateau and Virtual Learning Servers (VLS) such as WebEx. # When you set vleEnabled to true, you must also configure the VLS. See VLS Configuration Guide. # Setting Vle to true shows the VLS tabs in the administration environment. Default: false vleEnabled=false # When adHocEmailTemplateUsageEnabled is set to true, users can select a template in the Ad Hoc Notifications wizard. # When set to false, they cannot select a template. # This element only applies in an OnDemand license - Product license environments ignore it. Default: true. adHocEmailTemplateUsageEnabled=true # **** Learning Content Settings: Security Settings **** # # Enforce security on AICC content. For example, security does not allow # users to copy URLs to take over other user's AICC sessions. By default, set to false. # Note: since b1311 this flag is deprecated and no longer being used. Security has to be turned on for all AICC communications. aiccSecurityEnabled=true # Access-Control-Allow-Origin CORS header for the AICC endpoint PwsAicc # Enable it to allow AICC content hosted on a different domain (cross-domain content) to communicate with LMS server via Ajax, i.e XMLHttpRequest aiccAccessControlAllowOriginEnabled=false #specify your content server domain instead of * for better security, such as https://developer.mozilla.org aiccAccessControlAllowOriginHeader=* # Sets debugging pages for online support contentTestPagesEnabled=false # Enabling this setting stores the current User ID, name in the cookie. This information may be required for certain third party content # to work properly. Customers can enable this setting in that case. userIdentityInformationCookieEnabled=false # **** Learning Content Settings: Cross Domain Support Settings **** # # Cookie Cross domain support is used to support launching and tracking courseware from a different domain than the TMS domain. # TMS and the content server must however share the top level domain for cross domain tracking to be successful. # The value of cookieCrossDomainSupportDomainName is the top level domain. Thus an LMS with domain lms.plateausystems.com and a content server # with domain cms.plateausystems.com share the top level domain plateausystems.com. # Default of cookieCrossDomainSupportEnabled: false cookieCrossDomainSupportEnabled=false cookieCrossDomainSupportDomainName=plateausystems.com # Communication Cross domain support is used to support launching and tracking courseware from a different domain than the LMS. communicationCrossDomainSupportEnabled=false # The DefaultContentServerPath specifies the URI path where the TMS support files required by content reside on the content server. # Absolute URL can be specified, or else a URI path that is relative to the TMS base URL (must start with a slash). defaultContentServerPath=http://contentserver:7000/content contentWrapperPageName=main_content_wrapper.html scorm2004ContentWrapperPageName=scorm_2004_content_wrapper.html externalURLQuestionWrapperPageName=main_question_wrapper.html contentOpenerPageName=main_content_opener.html # The defaultProxletPath specifies the URI Path to Cross Domain Proxlet. This path does not include the Servlet mapping. # Absolute URL can be specified, or else a URI path that is relative to the TMS base URL (must start with a slash). defaultProxletPath=http://contentserver:7000/proxlet lmsSessionId=JSESSIONID #When set to true, item content structure is locked for any item that has at least one associated history record. Content cannot be added to, removed from or moved within a locked content structure. To enable editing of the content structure set to false. # WARNING: changes to the content structure could result in inability to review from history or inability to complete the course if not reassigned. lockItemContentStructure=false # ***************************************** # ******** BACKGROUND JOB SETTINGS ******** # ***************************************** ### **** Background Job Windows ***** # Background jobs are asynchronous jobs that an administrator can set up and pass to the Scheduler.  Background jobs can be scheduled # only during allowable time frames, described below with the allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes settings. Each allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes # element defines a window: a date and time during which administrators can run a background job. Make them times that the system is under light loads. # By default, each day is contained in brackets. '...[Monday].enabled' means that background jobs will run on Mondays. # However, the bracketed text is just a string to denote one window. You could also, for example create a [Weekdays] and [Weekends] window. # The default below one example of a non-day bracketed value, [Christmas]. # For each bracketed day, you can define start and end minutes, hours, dates, months, etc. A * means any of the unit. so if you have a * in minutes # and start/end hours between 0 and 5, then jobs can start on any minute between the hours of Midnight and 5 AM. # Note that hours are in 24-hour format so that 0 is Midnight and 13 is 1 PM. allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startDayofWeek=mon allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endDayofWeek=mon allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startDayofWeek=tue allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endDayofWeek=tue allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startDayofWeek=wed allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endDayofWeek=wed allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startDayofWeek=thu allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endDayofWeek=thu allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startDayofWeek=fri allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endDayofWeek=fri allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startDayofWeek=sat allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endDayofWeek=sat allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startDayofWeek=sun allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endDate=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endMonth=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endDayofWeek=sun allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startDate=25 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startMonth=12 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startDayofWeek=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endMinute=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endHour=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endDate=25 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endMonth=12 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endYear=* allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endDayofWeek=*  allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].startMinute=0 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].startHour=0 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].startDayofWeek=sat allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].endMinute=59 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].endHour=23 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].endDayofWeek=sat allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].enabled=true allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].startMinute=0 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].startHour=0 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].startDayofWeek=sun allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].endMinute=59 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].endHour=11 allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].endDayofWeek=sun  ### **** Limits and Timing in Background Jobs **** # lateTimeWindow sets a time expression (in minutes) that indicates the latest a timer trigger may fire past its scheduled firing time without being skipped. # For example, a late time window of \"30\" means that a job may fire up to thirty minutes late.  If the job is more than thirty minutes late, that job firing # is skipped. lateTimeWindow=30 # enableMakupFiring allows the last late firing to occur. For example, suppose a job is scheduled to fire once a day, the scheduler is down for a day, and the # late time window is small enough such that all these firings would be skipped when the engine begins running again. If makeup firings are not enabled, then # these late jobs will not fire. On the other hand, if makeup firings are enabled, then the last late job will fire. enableMakeupFiring=true # useItemLibraryBackgroundJob allows using background job for adding items to catalog. useItemLibraryBackgroundJob=false # Specifies the maximum number of e-mail messages that will be purged from mail archive at any one time. Default: 10000 emailArchivePurgeBatchCount=1000 # Specifying the batch size greater than 0 (zero) enables the processing of the records in batches. # This gives the ability to the user to commit the transaction after each batch has been processed. Default: 1000 numberOfRecordsToBeProcessedInABatch=1000 # Configuration for specific background/APM jobs.  Use Constants defined in the ApmConstants class for the background job names. # The job will be committed for every batch (transactionCommitSize), temporarily pausing for a number (sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches) of milliseconds # between jobs. apmJobSettings.TRNGEXPIRE.enabled=true apmJobSettings.TRNGEXPIRE.sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches=99 apmJobSettings.TRNGEXPIRE.transactionCommitSize=10000 apmJobSettings.EXTERNALREQUESTFORMDATAUPGRADER.enabled=true apmJobSettings.EXTERNALREQUESTFORMDATAUPGRADER.transactionCommitSize=500 apmJobSettings.ITEMJAMGROUPSNOTIFICATION.enabled=true apmJobSettings.ITEMJAMGROUPSNOTIFICATION.sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches=99 apmJobSettings.ITEMJAMGROUPSNOTIFICATION.transactionCommitSize=10000 apmJobSettings.USERHISTORYPURGE.enabled=true apmJobSettings.USERHISTORYPURGE.sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches=99 apmJobSettings.USERHISTORYPURGE.transactionCommitSize=100 # If the number of records that an operation operates on exceeds this count, the operation may have to be scheduled as a background job to run later instead of running online. # It is not recommended to choose a value greater than 100. # Assignment Profile jobs are also affected by the Assignment Profile Job specific settings below. onlineOperationMaxRecordsCount=5 # Defines the batch size for learning event resync commits.  0 - no limit. Default: 50. learningEventResynchronizationStudentCommitCount=50 # ### **** Settings Specific to the Assignment Profile Propagation and Synchronization Job **** # # The queries are batched and executed at one time. This setting determines how many queries are executed in one batch. Default: 1000 assignmentProfileBatchSize=1000 # Determines if operator data is read once and cached in memory or is re-read from the database during each background job. Default: true assignmentProfileMetaDataCache=true # Class implementing the AssignmentProfileQueryHelper interface used to generate query strings that determine which users should be # associated with an assignment profile.  Default: com.plateausystems.elms.bo.assignmentprofile.helper.AssignmentProfileQueryHelperImpl assignmentProfileQueryHelper=com.plateausystems.elms.bo.assignmentprofile.helper.AssignmentProfileQueryHelperImpl # The maximum number of records committed during any one transaction. Default: 100 assignmentProfileTxnCommitBatchSize=100 # ********************************************************* # ****** ALL USERS/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS ******* # ********************************************************* # These settings affect both the Admin and End User interaction. # **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Upload Limits **** # # fileUploadMaxSize is the maximum size in bytes for files uploaded to the server. It can be between 0 and 2147483647(2 GB). Default 10485760 bytes (10Mb) fileUploadMaxSize=10485760 # fileUploadFilenameMaxSize is the maximum amount of characters for a file name to be uploaded to the server. Default: 255 fileUploadFilenameMaxSize=255 # Settings specific to PQE, which is a module of Talent Management. # resourceUploadMaxSize is the limit, in bytes, of any image file uploaded to the server through PQE. # Question authors can change the \"size\" of an image file, but they are not changing the actual size in the database. # Rather, they are constraining the rendering size. Default: 524288. resourceUploadMaxSize=524288 # resourceUploadWarningSize is the limit, in bytes, of images that are uploaded to PQE without warning. # If the image size is over resourceUploadWarningSize, but below resourceUploadMaxSize, the question author is warned, # but not prevented from uploading the file.  Default: 262144 resourceUploadWarningSize=262144 # **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Privacy **** # # If hideUserPhotosGlobally is set to true all employee photos will be hidden EVERYWHERE in the application (admin and end user interfaces). Default: true hideUserPhotosGlobally=true # PrivacyAct Masks enable the student ID and/or the instructor ID to be hidden when a notification is sent # or when a report is printed. # Default mask. Admin running the report can change it at report time. Default: ********* privacyActDefaultMask=********* # Masks can be applied to notifications # Attribute module is the name of the module. When attribute enabled set to true, fields are masked in the module # By default, two modules are enabled: \"notification\" and \"report.\" privacyActMaskEnabled.Notification.StudentID=true privacyActMaskEnabled.Notification.InstructorID=true privacyActMaskEnabled.Report.StudentID=true privacyActMaskEnabled.Report.InstructorID=true # **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Error Checking and Reporting **** # # Set to true to show the stack trace to the user in browser (recommended for development and test environments). # Set to false (default setting) to only report ticket number to user in the browser (recommended for production environments). # Whether set to true or false, errors are always logged through Log4J with a ticket number (by default in the plateau.log file). reportStackTraceToUser=false # When emailValidationEnabled is set to true, the class in emailValidationClassName is called to validate e-mail syntax. # When a user types in an e-mail address, the system checks for @ symbols and periods (.) for correct e-mail syntax. Default: true. emailValidationEnabled=true # See JavaDoc for details about syntax checking in EmailValidationImpl # Default:com.plateausystems.elms.util.helper.EmailValidationImpl emailValidationClassName=com.plateausystems.elms.util.helper.EmailValidationImpl # **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Legacy Reports **** # # Set to true to show the legacy reports (reports defined with old report framework) in the report menus (both admin and end users). # Default: false showLegacyReports=false # ******************************************************************* # ******** END USER/APPLICATION INTERACTION BEHAVIOR **************** # ******************************************************************* ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Exam Settings *** # # Global setting whether to freeze the other component objects while the exam is in progress. # Default setting is true.  Set to false to allow \"open book\" tests. restrictAccessToOtherComponentObjectsDuringExam=true # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Learning Plan Configuration *** # # Set to true to show the Days Remaining Column rather than the Required by column in the Learning Plan Page and the Curriculum Details page. Default: false showDaysRemaining=false # Set to true to show the Assignment Type Column in the Learning Plan Page, the Curriculum Details page, and in the Home page. Default: false. showAssignmentType=false # learningPlanFieldsChooserItems controls the columns that users can enable and disable on the learning plan and some properties of the column. # The settings have attributes that identify the column, control the user interaction, call the column title, and control the width. # The attributes are: visibility - controls if user is forced to show column (mandatory), if column shows by default (default) # or if the column can be turned on or off by the user (optional) / titleLabelID - the label (from the I18N settings in the admin environment) # that appears at the top of the column / width - the default width of the column. learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.columnID=title learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.titleLabelID=label.Title learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.visibility=mandatory learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.width=50 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.columnID=itemID learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.titleLabelID=label.ID learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.visibility=optional learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.width=4 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.columnID=itemType learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.titleLabelID=label.Type learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.visibility=default learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.width=4 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.columnID=requiredBy learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.titleLabelID=label.RequiredBy learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.visibility=default learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.width=4 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.columnID=status learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.titleLabelID=label.Status learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.visibility=default learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.width=8 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.columnID=daysRemaining learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.titleLabelID=label.DaysRemaining learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.visibility=optional learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.width=4 learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.enabled=true learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.columnID=assignmentType learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.titleLabelID=label.AssignmentType learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.visibility=optional learningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.width=8 # The system default user learning plan settings. User can override with their own preferences # Defaults the Group By drop-down. Possible values: None, ItemType, AssignmentType,DueWithin, StatusTowardCompletion. Default: None learningPlanSystemPreferences.groupPlanFilter=None # Defaults the Filter By drop-down. Possible values: All, With Online Content, Registered, In progress Default: All learningPlanSystemPreferences.itemsFilter=All #  Defaults the Required By drop-down. Possible values: All, Next 30 Days, Next 60 Days, Next 90 Days. Default: All learningPlanSystemPreferences.requiredByFilter=All # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Home Page Settings *** # # Home Page Configuration to indicate which modules are displayed on the home page for users showHomeCatalogModule=true showHomeAlertsModule=true showHomeLearningPlanModule=true showHomeCareerPlanModule=true showHomeCurriculumModule=true showHomeNewItemModule=true showHomeFeaturedItemModule=true showHomeRevisedItemModule=true homeLearningPlanModuleRecordsToDisplay=5 homeCareerPlanModuleRecordsToDisplay=5 homeCurriculumModuleRecordsToDisplay=5 #homeFlaggedCatalogItemsToDisplay specifies the maximum number of flagged items and programs to display for EACH category (e.g. max 25 New, max 25 Revised, and max 25 Featured) homeFlaggedCatalogItemsToDisplay=25 # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Catalog Settings *** # # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Competency Search Settings *** # #This configuration is used for controlling whether on the competency search screen, users by default see all courses they have access to that are tied to the specified competencies, or #just the courses that match or exceed their current competency rating. #False: Users first see just the courses that match or exceed their current competency rating. View only items that help me close competency gaps is enabled by default on the competency search screen. #True: Users first see all courses they have access to that are tied to the specified competencies.View only items that help me close competency gaps is disabled by default on the competency search screen. showAllCoursesByDefault=false # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Calendar Settings *** # # ### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Persistence/Preferences *** # # Specify if the persistence can be lazy (does not have to happen immediately) and what class manages it. Default: true studentSubordinatesLazyPersistence=true studentSubordinatesPreferencesHandler=com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.StudentSubordinatesUIPreferencesHandler # The handler class that persists UI state preferences related to the user. # Default: com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.StudentUIPreferencesHandler studentUIPreferencesHandler=com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.StudentUIPreferencesHandler # When set to true the Show Pictures checkbox on the Dashboard / Succession Planner is selected by default. # If hideUserPhotosGlobally is set to true, then ShowPictures is irrelevant. Default: true studentSubordinatesShowPictures=true # When set to true the Show Status checkbox on Dashboard / Succession Planner is selected by default. Default: true studentSubordinatesShowStatus=true # ### ***** End User Interaction Behavior: Icon Preference *** # # Controls the icon preference on the end user interface. Default: true enableFontIcons=true # ### ***** End User Interaction Behavior: Miscellaneous *** # # This setting determines if the competency type is displayed to the user when competencies are displayed. showCompetencyType=true # talent search: max number of students per group talentPoolMaxGroupSize=1000 # This setting indicates the number of days from the current date to search for a new posts in the communities the user has access to. # This setting is used on the user's home page in the Communities button. Valid values are zero and any value greater than zero. searchNewPostsToCommunitiesInTheLastDays=14 # This setting would turn on or off the display of revision date time and number for items on the User's To-Do List. displayRevisionInformationInToDoList=false # This value is the number of reporting levels down displayed to a user and # should be an integer equal to or greater than 0. # Default: 0 # Example: #   If set to 0, the user will see all direct and indirect subordinates. #   If set to 1, the user will see their direct reports only. #   If set to 2, the user will see their direct reports and direct reports reporting into their direct reports and so on reportingLevelsToDisplay=0 # This configuration controls the display of the News page upon Login. Valid values are below (Values are case-sensitive): # Never : News page would not display on login. user would still have the ability to get to news page from the Easy link menu # Always : News page would always display on user login. User cannot dismiss this # UserDiscretion : News page would display upon login and the user would have the ability to not display each time. This is the default value displayNewsPageOnLogin=UserDiscretion # ********************************************************** # ******** ADMIN/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS ********** # ********************************************************** # ### **** Admin Application UI Behavior Configuration: Sticky Preferences **** # # Specify if the persistence can be lazy (does not have to happen immediately). Default: true userUILazyPersistence=true # This section is used for setting the handler class that will persist UI state preferences related to Tab Modes. # Default: com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.UserUIPreferencesHandler userUIPreferencesHandler=com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.UserUIPreferencesHandler # Defaults the administrator's view of users' learning plans. Administrator can set own preference. If the option is true # then, by default, dates are displayed in the User's preferred time zone. If false, it is displayed in the Admin's preferred time zone. Default: true learningPlanDisplayInLearnerTimezone=true # ### **** Admin Application UI Behavior Configuration: Limits **** # # The maximum rating an administrator is allowed to give a learning item. # Admins assign ratings on the Item Summary tab and can appear to end users in catalog. # Whether or not ratings appear in the catalog is controlled by the showItemRatingInCatalog property (CatalogConfiguration). maxItemRatingValue=5.0 # Limits the amount of copies that the Copy Scheduled Offering Wizard can make in the Admin Environment. # Limit applies to the amount of copies the admin can make any ONE time they run the wizard. # Setting a reasonable limit prevents admins from mistakenly overwhelming database. Default: 50 scheduleCopiesLimit=50 # Limits the amount of \"recents\" entries that can be seen on the Admin Recents Panel # Setting a reasonable limit prevents admins from overwhelming database. # Default Value\t: 50 / Min Value: 1 / Max Value: 100 maxNumberOfRecentsDisplayed=50 # ### **** Admin Application UI Behavior Configuration: Security/Self Modification *** # When restrictUserSelfModification is set to \"true\" administrators cannot change their own records. # For example, when set to true, an administrator \"jdoe\" with permissions to change administrator accounts, # can change all other administrator password and permissions *except* for his own. # Default value is true. We recommend true. Possible values are true or false. You might set to # false in development or training environments, for convenience. restrictUserSelfModification=true # ### **** User E-Signature PIN Self Reset Configuration *** # This configuration determines whether learners can reset their E-Signature PIN if they forget it. # By default, the property is set to true. When true, learners can use \"Forgot My PIN\" on the \"Options and Settings\" page to receive a secure email link, allowing them to create a new PIN. # When set to false, the \"Forgot My PIN\" option is hidden. enableESignatureResetPIN=true # This flag is used to order module tabs alphabetically. By default, it is true and module tabs will be displayed in alphabetical order # except for the Summary tab. Setting it to false will result in module tabs being ordered as they historically have been before this # configuration was introduced. displayModuleTabsInAlphabeticalOrder=true #This flag is used to enable the new supervisor enhancements for Assign/Remove learning, Record learning and Register/Witdraw Users. #The Old supervisor flow is deprecated. #Configuration options: true is the only valid option updatedSupervisorFlow=true #The maximum number of Users a Supervisor can register or withdraw using the Register / Withdraw Employees Wizard. The minimum value can be 1 and the maximum can be 1000. supervisorMaxUserRegisterWithdrawLimit=50 #This flag is used to enable the new tool for user Record learning. #The Old Self Record Learning flow is deprecated. #Configuration options: true is the only valid option updatedSelfRecordLearningFlow=true # ************************************************************************************************** # WARNING: No Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) filtering will be done if the URL is specified here as \"true\". # It is strongly recommended that you consult Plateau before modifying these values. xssFilterExcludedURLs[/globalErrorDispatcher.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editAppAdminStudent.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateAppAdminStudent.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateConfiguration.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editConfigurationSummary.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateSearchSelector.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editSearchSelector.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateUIDataSummary.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editUIDataSummary.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/addUIDataSummary.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/showSystemConfigurationReport.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/editPrintedExamTemplate.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/updatePrintedExamTemplate.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/getSecurityQuestion.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/references/updateOrg.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/references/editOrg.do]=true # XSS filtering for Notification Template messages can be turned on/off using the WEB_SECURITY configuration setting enableXSSFiltersForNotificationTemplateMessages. # The settings in this block control whether XSS filtering is applied to URLs related to Notification Template messages. # When these URLs are excluded from XSS filtering (=true), Notification Template messages will allow inclusion of IMG tags and special characters. # When these URLs are included in XSS filtering (=false), inclusion of IMG tags and special characters is disallowed. xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/previewNotificationTemplateMessages.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateNotificationTemplateMessages.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editNotificationTemplateMessages.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/listLabelNotificationTemplate.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/addNotificationTemplateMessage.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/sendNotificationAssistantStep5.do]=true xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/student/previewCertificateOfCompletion.do]=true # Enable to allow admin update locale labels with such as <li> html tags, when for instance the # secRules.specialCharsNotAllowed.enabled XSS filter is turned on. #xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/updateI18nActiveLocaleLabel.do]=true #request URL endings which can qualify the requests to be scanned xssFilterURLSuffix[.jsp]=true # These URLs which are outside of the regular *.jsp and *.do also need to be scanned xssFilterAdditionalURLs[/admin_acegi_authenticate]=true xssFilterAdditionalURLs[/student_acegi_authenticate]=true xssFilterAdditionalURLs[/site_acegi_authenticate]=true # Sets the login page behaviour to-remember or not-to-remember login crendentials. # Possible values are true/false. autoCompleteLoginForUser=true autoCompleteLoginForAdmin=true # This configuration is used to enable the online content early launch warning. This configuration # is added in b1207 # true: will enable the early launch warning. # false: will disable the early launch warning. enableOnlineContentEarlyLaunchWarning=true #This configuration specifies the threshold for online content launch warning and is only #applicable when the \"enableOnlineContentEarlyLaunchWarning\" is set to true. # The value is number of days and should be a positive integer greater than or equal to 0. onlineContentEarlyLaunchWarningThreshold=45 # ************************************************************************************************** # Opted in Features Related Settings # ************************************************************************************************** # This configuration is used to determine whether to use default password functionality or new initial random password generation. Added in b1207 # true: will enable random password generation for all the users created in our system. # false: will use default password functionality. enableRandomPasswordGenerationForNewUsers=false # This configuration is used to enable item and program recommendations feature. This is added in b1207 # true: will enable item and program recommedations feature. # false: will disable item and program recommendations feature. enableItemRecommendations=true # This configuration enforces the security domain restrictions set for the Edit Class permission when marking class attendance. The default value is false. # When set to true, any security domain restrictions for the Edit Class permission apply to marking class attendance. Only administrators with the necessary security domain permissions can mark attendance for classes. # When set to false, the security domain restrictions for the Edit Class permission don't apply to marking class attendance. Administrators with the Edit Class permission can mark attendance for classes, regardless of the configured security domain permissions. enforceSecurityDomainRestrictionForMarkingAttendance=false # ************************************************************************************************** # Peer Recommendation settings # ************************************************************************************************** # The Peer Recommendation would be hidden after the user has viewed the recommendation by navigating # to the Item / Program details page from the Recommendation tile and the entity has been added # to the Learning Plan or is part of the Learning History. This is to make the behavior # consistent with the Admin recommendations # This setting is deprecated and no longer used as of the 2H 2023 release. hideViewedP2PRecommendations=true # This configuration is the number of days after which a Peer Recommendation is deleted from the system. # After the number of configured days, a peer recommendation that has not been removed by the recipient will no longer appear in the peer recommendation section of the application. # The default value is 365 days. You can enter a value for this property only between 30 and 730 days. Revise the value to continue. peerRecommendationExpiration=365 # This configuration is used to choose the type of links to be included in the notification email. This is a system level configuration that is to be chosen based on the level of authentication needed. This is added in b1505 # true: will enable SmartLinks with personalized tokens for users to provide access without a login. # false: will provide a directlink to the recommended external link that requires a login to authenticate the user. enableSmartLinks=true # This configuration is used to enable multiple security questions for a user. This is added in b1210 enableMultipleSecurityQuestionsForUser=false # This configuration will enable or disable offline login page. offlinePlayerLoginRequired=true # This configuration controls whether Offline Player can be upgraded by users. # Warning: If this configuration is set to false, users will not be able to download the Offline Player from Options and Settings. offlinePlayerUpgradeEnabled=true #Local offline url for communications offlinePlayerLocalUrl=http://localhost:53759/learningoffline # If showItemThumbnailPhotosGlobally is set to false, the Thumbnail File and Thumbnail URL fields will be hidden from the admin interface for Item and Program records. If set to true, the thumbnail fields are displayed on the admin interface which allows an admin to override the system default for a specific Item or Program; Item also requires the fields to be displayed on the record configuration. Default: false showItemThumbnailPhotosGlobally=true # This configuration is used to determine maximum number of seats a supervisor can reserve while adding/editing a training requesting. Default: 500 # Setting a reasonable limit prevents admins from overwhelming database. # Default Value\t: 500 / Min Value: 1 / Max Value: 10000 maxNumberOfTrainingRequestSeats=100 # This configuration enables automatic assignment of training requests if the organization has been reviewed and either the seats requested equals seats granted # or the preselected user count is equal or less than the seats granted. Default: false. Possible values true/false autoAssignReviewedTrainingRequests=false # This configuration is used during the auto assignments of training requests, if the default assignment type is not provided for the items defaultAssignmentTypeForAutoAssignTrainingRequests= # showSystemDefaultThumbnail decides whether the default thumbnail style is a photo (true) or an icon (false). Note that the system default thumbnail can be overridden for most learning at System Admin>Configuration>Images. showSystemDefaultThumbnail=true # This configuration is used to enable HTML descriptions. Default: false enableHTMLDescriptions=true # Setting the allowFutureHireDates property to true enables the creation/update of user records with a future hire date. Default: false # Setting it back to false prevents the creation/update of user records with a future hire date but does not perform any data cleanup on existing records. allowFutureHireDates=false # Setting the enableCappingFactor to true enables Capping Factor feature.This will make the learning event recorder to display system default currency instead of the drop-down.It wont allow to change the currency for addition costs in Learning Event Editor. This will also hide Training days while recording learning. Default: false enableCappingFactor=false # This configuration is used to enable/disable the notification header and footer support. enableNotificationHeaderFooter=false # This configuration is used to set the maximum number of days that an admin is able to download their export # file results in the data export tool.  After the number of configured days, the admin will no longer be able # to access the export results. The allowable range is between 1-30 days.  Recommended default setting is 3. exportExpiration=3 # This flag is used to allow if admins can enter/modify data in the registration form custom columns when registering/modifying users enrollment allowAdminToModifyRegistrationFormCustomColumns=true allowSupervisorToEnterRegistrationFormCustomColumnsData=true allowUserToModifyCustomColumnsDataIfRegisteredBySuper=false allowUserToModifyCustomColumnsDataIfRegisteredByAdmin=false # This configuration specifies the maximum number of subordinates displayed under any node, including the top-level nodes when displaying employees in the \"My Team\" tree-view maxNumberOfSubordinatesDisplayedInTree=300 # The following configuration allows the admin to identify whether or not users can submit incomplete surveys for surveys that are set as \"optional\". This setting applies to # both Item Evaluation and Follow-up Evaluation survey types UsersCanSubmitIncompleteOptionalSurveys=false #Enables the Manage Learning Tool from a scheduled offering. manageLearningToolEnabled=false # This configuration allows the publishing of events to the Service Event Bus (SEB) to be enabled or disabled, based on the SEB-supported event type. #If the destination is unavailable at the time the event is published to the SEB, the event publication fails. You can enable rerunFailedSebPublishedEvents to process the failed events from previous days. You can rerun events for up to 30 days prior to the current day. The number of prior days to reprocess is set in numberOfPriorDaysToRerunSebPublishedEvents. sebPublishedEventTypes[LearningCompletion]=false rerunFailedSebPublishedEvents=false numberOfPriorDaysToRerunSebPublishedEvents=1 # When set to true, if a self-registering user provides an email address, the system will not register the user unless that email address is unique across all users of the system selfRegistrationUniqueEmailAddressRequired=false # This configuration can be used to indicate whether the LMS instance is integrated with Jam or not. # (Note: this property replaces the previously used 'enableSocialTabInCatalogSearch' property.) # true: Indicates that Jam integration available and enabled # false: Indicates that Jam integration is not available or disabled jamIntegrationEnabled=false #When set to true, the from field of the email notification will be replaced with the the recipient's org email. useOrgEmailAsFromForNotifications=false #This configuration is dependent on Course Home being enabled (enableCourseHomeBlended=true). #When set to true, content will always launch inline, regardless of the content-level setting. #When set to false, the content-level setting determines the launch method. #Default value is false. overrideContentLaunchInNewWindow=false #This configuration will enable the content object Audit #When set to true , new field(enable_content_audit) is visible on item snapshot for online and blended courses #when enable_content_audit is set to true , the content communication is saved to Audit table i.e., PA_CBT_STUD_CPNT_MOD_AUDIT enableContentObjectAuditTrail=false # This property applies to the new Learning experience to show or hide the Required Learning section. The default value is set to false. # If no required courses are assigned to users, and you want to hide the section for them, set the property to true. This property applies to specific organizations and user groups where the section is set to be hidden. #When hideRequiredLearningSectionOnLearningPortal is set to true, users do not see the Required Learning section on their Learning Portal. Note that when there is content on the Required Learning section, setting the property to true does not hide the section on users' Learning Portal. #When hideRequiredLearningSectionOnLearningPortal is set to false, the Required Learning section appears on the users' Learning Portal. hideRequiredLearningSectionOnLearningPortal=false # When this configuration is enabled, the Purge Deleted User Audit # History APM will add a list of the purged users to PA_USER_PURGE_LOG. # Disabling this configuration does not delete any previously added records. # WARNING: Enabling purge logging will prevent reusing a purged User ID in the future. enablePurgeLog=false # This KBA feature depends on the System Setting enableErrorFingerprinting JVM flag. # If the enableErrorFingerprinting flag is false, this setting will be considered as false always. # Set it to false to opt out enableKBASearchService=true # When this configuration is enabled, the user can view the Learning History of all Employments. # Set the learningHistoryOfAllEmployments flag as false to opt out. learningHistoryOfAllEmployments=false # For customers integrated with Talent Intelligence Hub, setting this configuration to true allows users to view the legacy 'Competencies' entity in the menu, in addition to the 'Attributes' entity. # The competency search selector functionality remains the same. showCompetenciesMenuAfterTalentIntelligenceHubMigration=false #This configuration prevents intermittent early completion issues for SCORM 2004 4th edition content that occur when a learner navigates away from or exits content. #When set to true, this configuration assumes that the completionSetByContent and objectiveSetByContent values in the content manifest are true, so Learning records completion only after the content communicates completion. #The default value is false and the setting values in the content manifest determine how content completion is communicated. contentCommunicatesCompletion=true #This configuration allows the continued use of unload browser events for online content and is enabled (true) by default. # This temporary setting is intended to allow customers additional time to replace unload browser events for their online content and will only be available until Google deprecates support in 2025. enableContentUnloadEventUsage=true #This configuration is specific to ILX and decides the behaviour of primary actions related to Launch Course on ILX cards #When set to true, the primary actions related to Launch Course would redirect to Course Home page. #When set to false, the primary actions related to Launch Course would redirect directly to Course Launch. navigateToCourseHomeForILXLaunchCourseActions=false #The configuration determines whether additional details for learning cards, such as learning ID, rating, description, associated skills, and other metadata, are shown in the \"Details\" popover when a learner selects a learning card on the new Learning home page. #The default is set to true, where the \"Details\" popover appears with the additional information for a learning. #When set to false, learners are redirected to the \"Course Home\" page, without displaying the popover. displayAdditionalDetailsForLearningCards=true #The configuration determines whether deleting iContent files using the iContent Management tool also removes the content structure from its linked courses. The default value is set to false. #When set to false, deleting files retains the content structure in all associated courses. You need to manually remove the deleted content from the structure and reactivate the course. #When set to true, deleting files automatically removes the content structure from all associated courses. While the remaining content is still accessible, it is no longer linked to the course. removeContentStructureOnDelete=false #The configuration determines whether learners can access the redesigned \"Program Details\", \"Curriculum Details\" and \"Curricula Status\" pages from the Learning home page. #The default is false where learners continue to access the legacy pages. #Set it to true for learners to access the redesigned pages. enableLegacyUIReplacement=true  # This configuration controls whether the user should be allowed to access course in a program which has approvals. # When set to false (default), users are not restricted from accessing courses in programs with approvals. # When set to true, the system enforces approval requirements for accessing courses in programs. honorApprovalsForPrograms=true  # This configuration controls whether the system honors prerequisites when managing learning programs. # When set to true, the system enforces prerequisite requirements for program enrollment and completion. # When set to false, prerequisite enforcement is disabled, allowing users to access programs without meeting prerequisites. honorPrerequisitesForPrograms=true"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl name=\"# This configuration contains system administrator information r*\" role=\"cell\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"name":"# This configuration contains system administrator information r*","role":"cell","aastate":"opaque"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl name=\"Konfigurasjon\" role=\"editable text\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"name":"Konfigurasjon","role":"editable text","aastate":"fokuserbar, editable, multiline, opaque, selectable text","text":"# This configuration contains system administrator information required to configure the Talent Management application.\n# It is divided into sections to group the concerns:\n#    SYSTEM: Contains settings for TMS Globally (and not a particular module)\n#    I18N BEHAVIOR: Contains settings for the internationalization system of Talent Management\n#    HELP SYSTEM: Contains settings for the help system of Talent Management\n#    LEARNING CONTENT: Contains settings for the delivery of learning content to users\n#    BACKGROUND JOB: Contains settings for background job processing\n#    ALL USERS/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS: Contains settings to control how all users (both admin and end) interact with the application\n#    END USERS/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS: Contains settings to control how end users interact with the application\n#    ADMIN/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS: Contains settings to control how administrators interact with the application\n# ****************************************\n# *********** SYSTEM SETTINGS ************\n# ****************************************\n# **** System Settings: Encryption Settings ****\n# The following encryption uses the JavaTM Cryptography Architecture.\n# Changing any of these values will cause all encrypted data in the database to be re-encrypted using the new settings.\n# See the documentation for more details on this section.\nencryption.className=com.plateausystems.elms.util.helper.ElmsJceEncryption\n# The encryption provider. The default is Sun JCE, but any JCE provider can be used.\nencryption.provider=SunJCE\n# The encryption algorithm used to encrypt data. The default is Triple-DES (a.k.a. DESede), although any secret\n# key encryption provider supported by JCE is supported here (DESede, AES, Blowfish, etc).\n# DES is not to be used as it is consider to be weak.\nencryption.algorithm=DESede\n# As of TMS 6.2.3, the encryption key is now a wrapped key value (so the value of encryption.key below may look\n# like it is a new value but actually it just represents a wrapped version of the original encryption key).\n# If you have never changed the value of the encryption.key setting, and you are upgrading to 6.2.3 or later,\n# use the encryption.key value provided here (rather than the old key which ended in \"==\").\n# For extra security, a new random key value can be obtained with the JceEncryption command-line utility.\n# For even extra security, you can install the JCE Unlimited Strength Jurisdiction Policy Files 6 and use keys larger than 128-bit.\nencryption.key=*****\nencryption.mode=\nencryption.padding=\n# **** System Settings: Database Preferences ****\n# Do NOT change database preferences after initial set up of your system.\n# Java date and time pattern. Use Java Simple Date format\ndbPreferencesDatePattern.pattern=MM/dd/yyyy\ndbPreferencesTimePattern.pattern=hh:mm:ss aaa\ndbPreferencesLanguageCode=en\ndbPreferencesCountryCode=US\n# SQL date and time pattern used to form the SQL for the particular database;\n# needs to match with the above patterns. Use Oracle Datetime format syntax.\ndbDatePattern=mm/dd/yyyy\ndbTimePattern=hh:mi:ss AM\n#  This is maximum year value for a date. This value depends on the deployed database. Default: 9999\nmaxDbSupportedYear=9999\n# **** System Settings: Validation Settings ****\n# Defines limits to the size (positive and negative) of numbers, by type.\n# Properties minValue and maxValue hold the min and the max for numbers of their type (minLongValue is for Long type, for example)\n# Long default: min: -9999999999  max: 9999999999\nminLongValue=-9999999999\nmaxLongValue=9999999999\n# Double default: min: -9999999999.00 max: 9999999999.00\nminDoubleValue=-9999999999.00\nmaxDoubleValue=9999999999.00\n# **** System Settings: Caching ****\n# Inserts scripts to control the caching of pages by the browser. The property proxyCaching controls caching for Microsoft Internet Explorer.\n# The property nsBrowserCaching controls the caching for Mozilla browsers. By default, both are set to false.\nproxyCaching=false\nnsBrowserCaching=false\n# **** System Settings: Web Services ****\n# Set the webServicesenabled property to true if you want the Web Services to be accessible. Default: false.\n# Web Services are also enabled if successfactorsLearningEnabled is also set to true in SuccessFactorsLearningConfiguration even if the setting here is false\nwebServicesEnabled=false\n# ****************************************\n# ******** I18N BEHAVIOR SETTINGS ********\n# ****************************************\n# These settings configure the behavior of the application when a label is requested but is not found in the locale label cache.\n# If logging is desired, isI18nLabelExceptionLoggingEnabled should be enabled (set to true) and the log4j configuration file can be tweaked as desired\n# (defaults to a separate missinglabels.log file in the logs folder).  If desired, a stack trace can also be spit out for missing\n# label detection up to a depth specified in the stackTraceDepthForMissingLabelLogging.  If this attribute is missing or zero, no\n# stack trace will be output with the error message logged for the missing label.\nisI18nLabelExceptionLoggingEnabled=false\nstackTraceDepthForMissingLabelLogging=7\n#This configuration is used to show/hide the locale selector for an unauthenticated user in the system default header when more than one active locale exists.\nshowPreferenceSelectorInDefaultHeader=false\n#This is only for V1 label cache\n# Once a label has been determined not to be in the cached label set, the default behavior of the application is to check the DB\n# again to see if the label was added since the last label cache read.  This can be turned OFF by setting the enabled attribute\n# of the allowRepeatedDBLookups property to false.  Otherwise, the i18nMissingLabelStatusTTL attribute is the number of milliseconds to\n# wait for any given label between DB lookups.  This can improve performance at the cost of a temporarily stale missing label\n# by preventing too many DB lookups for the same missing label.  If zero, there is no delay - all missing label lookups\n# go to the DB each time.  This would be useful in a development phase of the application.  However, for production it is recommended\n# to give this value an acceptable time to wait for labels to be loaded.  Default recommendation is 10 minutes (600,000 milliseconds).\nallowRepeatedDBLookups=true\ni18nMissingLabelStatusTTL=600000\n#This is only for V1 label cache\n# If all labels added post-production begin with a known set of prefixes, use this section to configure those known prefixes\n# so that the DB lookup processing for missing labels is fine-tuned to apply to only labels matching these \"starts-with\"\n# patterns.  For each bracketed value, the value of the element becomes a case-sensitive pattern\n# matched against a missing label ID.  If the label ID starts with any of the patterns listed here, it is eligible for another\n# DB lookup after the i18nMissingLabelStatusTTL has elapsed.\nallowRepeatedDBLookupsForLabelsStartingWith[label.u.]=true\n# **************************************\n# ******** HELP SYSTEM SETTINGS ********\n# **************************************\n# Configure baseHelpRedirectURL to point to the location where the help.war file is deployed.\n# By default this is a WAR file inside of the TMS package (webapps folder), so the context path is simply /help.\n# If deployed outside the EAR, you should give a complete URL, e.g. http://www.plateau.com/TMSHelp\n# The helpRedirectorURI is the URI (/contextPath/redirectorURI?params...) that will be used for initial help links.\n# Change the helpRedirectorURI only if you change the struts action or want to go through a custom redirector\nbaseHelpRedirectURL=/help\nhelpRedirectorURI=/getHelpRedirector.do\n# ********************************************\n# ******** LEARNING CONTENT SETTINGS *********\n# ********************************************\n#\n# **** Learning Content Settings: Content ****\n#\n# Servlet mapping for the PwsAiccServlet, external AICC courseware will send HTTP message to this URL\n# PwsAicc Servlet tracks the completion of external AICC content through HTTP messages.\naiccReturnURL=/PwsAicc\n# Window options when launching different course types.\ncontentWindowOpenOptions.aicc=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1\ncontentWindowOpenOptions.scorm=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1\ncontentWindowOpenOptions.browser=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1\ncontentWindowOpenOptions.document=width=800,height=600,top=0,left=0,toolbar=0,location=0,directories=0,status=1,menubar=0,scrollbars=1,resizable=1\n# When content is opened inline in the same browser window, the size of the IFrame that\n# contains the content is controlled by these settings. You can set different sizes for each\n# launch method that supports opening a content object inline. The configuration is specified # as an integer percentage value (20-100) of the parent browser window size.\n# If a value is not specified it will default to 80\ninlineContentWindowSize.aicc.width=80\ninlineContentWindowSize.aicc.height=80\ninlineContentWindowSize.scorm.width=80\ninlineContentWindowSize.scorm.height=80\ninlineContentWindowSize.browser.width=80\ninlineContentWindowSize.browser.height=80\n# Servlet mapping for the PwsTrackingFuncitonsServlet, the tracking applet will send HTTP message to this URL\n# PwsTrackingFunction Servlet tracks the completion of Plateau Structured content. Default: /PwsTrackingFunction\ncontentTrackingFunctionReturnURL=/PwsTrackingFunction\n# Servlet mapping for the SCORM 2004 RTE Servlet, the PlateauSCORM2004API applet will send HTTP message to this URL\n# SCORM 2004 RTE tracks the completion of SCORM 2004 content. Default: /ScormRteServlet\nscorm2004ReturnURL=/ScormRteServlet\n# Servlet mapping for the PwsStudentExamApi, the Exam Question will send HTTP message to this URL.\n# PwsStudentExamApi tracks exam completion. Default: /PwsStudentExamApi\nexamQuestionReturnURL=/PwsStudentExamApi\n# The Online Content Structure page expires after being idle for this amount of time (in seconds)\n# The expired page transitions to a page that supports content communication (AICC and SCORM).\n#   When the user returns to the Online Content Structure page it is updated with content statuses. Default: 120\ncontentStructurePageExpireDuration=120\n# The Online Content Structure page has a LMSsession keep alive feature that is based on this amount of time (in seconds).\n# Default: 300 (5 min)\n# 0 - Session timeout-600 (i.e. 10 minutes based on the 30 min session time out);  Minimum : 120 (i.e. 2 minutes)\ncontentStructurePageKeepAliveInterval=300\n# This is an opt in setting to extend the User session to 4 hours while taking the AICC content.\n# It will reset back to normal however when user navigates back to the home page, i.e. away from the content launching page.\nextendAiccOnlineSession=false\n# The maximum number of resources that will be cached by the PexamResorceServlet. Default: 100\nexamResourceCacheMaxCount=100\n# **** Learning Content Settings: Learning Component Settings ****\n#\n# The Vle element enables connection between Plateau and Virtual Learning Servers (VLS) such as WebEx.\n# When you set vleEnabled to true, you must also configure the VLS. See VLS Configuration Guide.\n# Setting Vle to true shows the VLS tabs in the administration environment. Default: false\nvleEnabled=false\n# When adHocEmailTemplateUsageEnabled is set to true, users can select a template in the Ad Hoc Notifications wizard.\n# When set to false, they cannot select a template.\n# This element only applies in an OnDemand license - Product license environments ignore it. Default: true.\nadHocEmailTemplateUsageEnabled=true\n# **** Learning Content Settings: Security Settings ****\n#\n# Enforce security on AICC content. For example, security does not allow\n# users to copy URLs to take over other user's AICC sessions. By default, set to false.\n# Note: since b1311 this flag is deprecated and no longer being used. Security has to be turned on for all AICC communications.\naiccSecurityEnabled=true\n# Access-Control-Allow-Origin CORS header for the AICC endpoint PwsAicc\n# Enable it to allow AICC content hosted on a different domain (cross-domain content) to communicate with LMS server via Ajax, i.e XMLHttpRequest\naiccAccessControlAllowOriginEnabled=false\n#specify your content server domain instead of * for better security, such as https://developer.mozilla.org\naiccAccessControlAllowOriginHeader=*\n# Sets debugging pages for online support\ncontentTestPagesEnabled=false\n# Enabling this setting stores the current User ID, name in the cookie. This information may be required for certain third party content\n# to work properly. Customers can enable this setting in that case.\nuserIdentityInformationCookieEnabled=false\n# **** Learning Content Settings: Cross Domain Support Settings ****\n#\n# Cookie Cross domain support is used to support launching and tracking courseware from a different domain than the TMS domain.\n# TMS and the content server must however share the top level domain for cross domain tracking to be successful.\n# The value of cookieCrossDomainSupportDomainName is the top level domain. Thus an LMS with domain lms.plateausystems.com and a content server\n# with domain cms.plateausystems.com share the top level domain plateausystems.com.\n# Default of cookieCrossDomainSupportEnabled: false\ncookieCrossDomainSupportEnabled=false\ncookieCrossDomainSupportDomainName=plateausystems.com\n# Communication Cross domain support is used to support launching and tracking courseware from a different domain than the LMS.\ncommunicationCrossDomainSupportEnabled=false\n# The DefaultContentServerPath specifies the URI path where the TMS support files required by content reside on the content server.\n# Absolute URL can be specified, or else a URI path that is relative to the TMS base URL (must start with a slash).\ndefaultContentServerPath=http://contentserver:7000/content\ncontentWrapperPageName=main_content_wrapper.html\nscorm2004ContentWrapperPageName=scorm_2004_content_wrapper.html\nexternalURLQuestionWrapperPageName=main_question_wrapper.html\ncontentOpenerPageName=main_content_opener.html\n# The defaultProxletPath specifies the URI Path to Cross Domain Proxlet. This path does not include the Servlet mapping.\n# Absolute URL can be specified, or else a URI path that is relative to the TMS base URL (must start with a slash).\ndefaultProxletPath=http://contentserver:7000/proxlet\nlmsSessionId=JSESSIONID\n#When set to true, item content structure is locked for any item that has at least one associated history record. Content cannot be added to, removed from or moved within a locked content structure. To enable editing of the content structure set to false.\n# WARNING: changes to the content structure could result in inability to review from history or inability to complete the course if not reassigned.\nlockItemContentStructure=false\n# *****************************************\n# ******** BACKGROUND JOB SETTINGS ********\n# *****************************************\n### **** Background Job Windows *****\n# Background jobs are asynchronous jobs that an administrator can set up and pass to the Scheduler.  Background jobs can be scheduled\n# only during allowable time frames, described below with the allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes settings. Each allowableBackgroundJobTimeframes\n# element defines a window: a date and time during which administrators can run a background job. Make them times that the system is under light loads.\n# By default, each day is contained in brackets. '...[Monday].enabled' means that background jobs will run on Mondays.\n# However, the bracketed text is just a string to denote one window. You could also, for example create a [Weekdays] and [Weekends] window.\n# The default below one example of a non-day bracketed value, [Christmas].\n# For each bracketed day, you can define start and end minutes, hours, dates, months, etc. A * means any of the unit. so if you have a * in minutes\n# and start/end hours between 0 and 5, then jobs can start on any minute between the hours of Midnight and 5 AM.\n# Note that hours are in 24-hour format so that 0 is Midnight and 13 is 1 PM.\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].startDayofWeek=mon\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Monday].endDayofWeek=mon\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].startDayofWeek=tue\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Tuesday].endDayofWeek=tue\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].startDayofWeek=wed\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Wednesday].endDayofWeek=wed\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].startDayofWeek=thu\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Thursday].endDayofWeek=thu\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].startDayofWeek=fri\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Friday].endDayofWeek=fri\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].startDayofWeek=sat\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Saturday].endDayofWeek=sat\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].startDayofWeek=sun\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endDate=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endMonth=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Sunday].endDayofWeek=sun\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startDate=25\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startMonth=12\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]startDayofWeek=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endMinute=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endHour=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endDate=25\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endMonth=12\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endYear=*\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[Christmas]endDayofWeek=*\n\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].startMinute=0\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].startHour=0\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].startDayofWeek=sat\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].endMinute=59\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].endHour=23\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Saturday].endDayofWeek=sat\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].enabled=true\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].startMinute=0\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].startHour=0\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].startDayofWeek=sun\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].endMinute=59\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].endHour=11\nallowableBackgroundJobTimeframes[IContent_Sunday].endDayofWeek=sun\n\n### **** Limits and Timing in Background Jobs ****\n# lateTimeWindow sets a time expression (in minutes) that indicates the latest a timer trigger may fire past its scheduled firing time without being skipped.\n# For example, a late time window of \"30\" means that a job may fire up to thirty minutes late.  If the job is more than thirty minutes late, that job firing\n# is skipped.\nlateTimeWindow=30\n# enableMakupFiring allows the last late firing to occur. For example, suppose a job is scheduled to fire once a day, the scheduler is down for a day, and the\n# late time window is small enough such that all these firings would be skipped when the engine begins running again. If makeup firings are not enabled, then\n# these late jobs will not fire. On the other hand, if makeup firings are enabled, then the last late job will fire.\nenableMakeupFiring=true\n# useItemLibraryBackgroundJob allows using background job for adding items to catalog.\nuseItemLibraryBackgroundJob=false\n# Specifies the maximum number of e-mail messages that will be purged from mail archive at any one time. Default: 10000\nemailArchivePurgeBatchCount=1000\n# Specifying the batch size greater than 0 (zero) enables the processing of the records in batches.\n# This gives the ability to the user to commit the transaction after each batch has been processed. Default: 1000\nnumberOfRecordsToBeProcessedInABatch=1000\n# Configuration for specific background/APM jobs.  Use Constants defined in the ApmConstants class for the background job names.\n# The job will be committed for every batch (transactionCommitSize), temporarily pausing for a number (sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches) of milliseconds\n# between jobs.\napmJobSettings.TRNGEXPIRE.enabled=true\napmJobSettings.TRNGEXPIRE.sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches=99\napmJobSettings.TRNGEXPIRE.transactionCommitSize=10000\napmJobSettings.EXTERNALREQUESTFORMDATAUPGRADER.enabled=true\napmJobSettings.EXTERNALREQUESTFORMDATAUPGRADER.transactionCommitSize=500\napmJobSettings.ITEMJAMGROUPSNOTIFICATION.enabled=true\napmJobSettings.ITEMJAMGROUPSNOTIFICATION.sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches=99\napmJobSettings.ITEMJAMGROUPSNOTIFICATION.transactionCommitSize=10000\napmJobSettings.USERHISTORYPURGE.enabled=true\napmJobSettings.USERHISTORYPURGE.sleepMilliSecondsBetweenBatches=99\napmJobSettings.USERHISTORYPURGE.transactionCommitSize=100\n# If the number of records that an operation operates on exceeds this count, the operation may have to be scheduled as a background job to run later instead of running online.\n# It is not recommended to choose a value greater than 100.\n# Assignment Profile jobs are also affected by the Assignment Profile Job specific settings below.\nonlineOperationMaxRecordsCount=5\n# Defines the batch size for learning event resync commits.  0 - no limit. Default: 50.\nlearningEventResynchronizationStudentCommitCount=50\n#\n### **** Settings Specific to the Assignment Profile Propagation and Synchronization Job ****\n#\n# The queries are batched and executed at one time. This setting determines how many queries are executed in one batch. Default: 1000\nassignmentProfileBatchSize=1000\n# Determines if operator data is read once and cached in memory or is re-read from the database during each background job. Default: true\nassignmentProfileMetaDataCache=true\n# Class implementing the AssignmentProfileQueryHelper interface used to generate query strings that determine which users should be\n# associated with an assignment profile.  Default: com.plateausystems.elms.bo.assignmentprofile.helper.AssignmentProfileQueryHelperImpl\nassignmentProfileQueryHelper=com.plateausystems.elms.bo.assignmentprofile.helper.AssignmentProfileQueryHelperImpl\n# The maximum number of records committed during any one transaction. Default: 100\nassignmentProfileTxnCommitBatchSize=100\n# *********************************************************\n# ****** ALL USERS/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS *******\n# *********************************************************\n# These settings affect both the Admin and End User interaction.\n# **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Upload Limits ****\n#\n# fileUploadMaxSize is the maximum size in bytes for files uploaded to the server. It can be between 0 and 2147483647(2 GB). Default 10485760 bytes (10Mb)\nfileUploadMaxSize=10485760\n# fileUploadFilenameMaxSize is the maximum amount of characters for a file name to be uploaded to the server. Default: 255\nfileUploadFilenameMaxSize=255\n# Settings specific to PQE, which is a module of Talent Management.\n# resourceUploadMaxSize is the limit, in bytes, of any image file uploaded to the server through PQE.\n# Question authors can change the \"size\" of an image file, but they are not changing the actual size in the database.\n# Rather, they are constraining the rendering size. Default: 524288.\nresourceUploadMaxSize=524288\n# resourceUploadWarningSize is the limit, in bytes, of images that are uploaded to PQE without warning.\n# If the image size is over resourceUploadWarningSize, but below resourceUploadMaxSize, the question author is warned,\n# but not prevented from uploading the file.  Default: 262144\nresourceUploadWarningSize=262144\n# **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Privacy ****\n#\n# If hideUserPhotosGlobally is set to true all employee photos will be hidden EVERYWHERE in the application (admin and end user interfaces). Default: true\nhideUserPhotosGlobally=true\n# PrivacyAct Masks enable the student ID and/or the instructor ID to be hidden when a notification is sent\n# or when a report is printed.\n# Default mask. Admin running the report can change it at report time. Default: *********\nprivacyActDefaultMask=*********\n# Masks can be applied to notifications\n# Attribute module is the name of the module. When attribute enabled set to true, fields are masked in the module\n# By default, two modules are enabled: \"notification\" and \"report.\"\nprivacyActMaskEnabled.Notification.StudentID=true\nprivacyActMaskEnabled.Notification.InstructorID=true\nprivacyActMaskEnabled.Report.StudentID=true\nprivacyActMaskEnabled.Report.InstructorID=true\n# **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Error Checking and Reporting ****\n#\n# Set to true to show the stack trace to the user in browser (recommended for development and test environments).\n# Set to false (default setting) to only report ticket number to user in the browser (recommended for production environments).\n# Whether set to true or false, errors are always logged through Log4J with a ticket number (by default in the plateau.log file).\nreportStackTraceToUser=false\n# When emailValidationEnabled is set to true, the class in emailValidationClassName is called to validate e-mail syntax.\n# When a user types in an e-mail address, the system checks for @ symbols and periods (.) for correct e-mail syntax. Default: true.\nemailValidationEnabled=true\n# See JavaDoc for details about syntax checking in EmailValidationImpl\n# Default:com.plateausystems.elms.util.helper.EmailValidationImpl\nemailValidationClassName=com.plateausystems.elms.util.helper.EmailValidationImpl\n# **** Global Application Interaction Settings: Legacy Reports ****\n#\n# Set to true to show the legacy reports (reports defined with old report framework) in the report menus (both admin and end users).\n# Default: false\nshowLegacyReports=false\n# *******************************************************************\n# ******** END USER/APPLICATION INTERACTION BEHAVIOR ****************\n# *******************************************************************\n### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Exam Settings ***\n#\n# Global setting whether to freeze the other component objects while the exam is in progress.\n# Default setting is true.  Set to false to allow \"open book\" tests.\nrestrictAccessToOtherComponentObjectsDuringExam=true\n#\n### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Learning Plan Configuration ***\n#\n# Set to true to show the Days Remaining Column rather than the Required by column in the Learning Plan Page and the Curriculum Details page. Default: false\nshowDaysRemaining=false\n# Set to true to show the Assignment Type Column in the Learning Plan Page, the Curriculum Details page, and in the Home page. Default: false.\nshowAssignmentType=false\n# learningPlanFieldsChooserItems controls the columns that users can enable and disable on the learning plan and some properties of the column.\n# The settings have attributes that identify the column, control the user interaction, call the column title, and control the width.\n# The attributes are: visibility - controls if user is forced to show column (mandatory), if column shows by default (default)\n# or if the column can be turned on or off by the user (optional) / titleLabelID - the label (from the I18N settings in the admin environment)\n# that appears at the top of the column / width - the default width of the column.\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.enabled=true\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.columnID=title\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.titleLabelID=label.Title\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.visibility=mandatory\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.title.width=50\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.enabled=true\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.columnID=itemID\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.titleLabelID=label.ID\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.visibility=optional\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemID.width=4\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.enabled=true\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.columnID=itemType\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.titleLabelID=label.Type\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.visibility=default\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.itemType.width=4\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.enabled=true\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.columnID=requiredBy\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.titleLabelID=label.RequiredBy\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.visibility=default\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.requiredBy.width=4\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.enabled=true\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.columnID=status\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.titleLabelID=label.Status\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.visibility=default\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.status.width=8\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.enabled=true\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.columnID=daysRemaining\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.titleLabelID=label.DaysRemaining\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.visibility=optional\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.daysRemaining.width=4\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.enabled=true\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.columnID=assignmentType\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.titleLabelID=label.AssignmentType\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.visibility=optional\nlearningPlanFieldsChooserItems.assignmentType.width=8\n# The system default user learning plan settings. User can override with their own preferences\n# Defaults the Group By drop-down. Possible values: None, ItemType, AssignmentType,DueWithin, StatusTowardCompletion. Default: None\nlearningPlanSystemPreferences.groupPlanFilter=None\n# Defaults the Filter By drop-down. Possible values: All, With Online Content, Registered, In progress Default: All\nlearningPlanSystemPreferences.itemsFilter=All\n#  Defaults the Required By drop-down. Possible values: All, Next 30 Days, Next 60 Days, Next 90 Days. Default: All\nlearningPlanSystemPreferences.requiredByFilter=All\n#\n### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Home Page Settings ***\n#\n# Home Page Configuration to indicate which modules are displayed on the home page for users\nshowHomeCatalogModule=true\nshowHomeAlertsModule=true\nshowHomeLearningPlanModule=true\nshowHomeCareerPlanModule=true\nshowHomeCurriculumModule=true\nshowHomeNewItemModule=true\nshowHomeFeaturedItemModule=true\nshowHomeRevisedItemModule=true\nhomeLearningPlanModuleRecordsToDisplay=5\nhomeCareerPlanModuleRecordsToDisplay=5\nhomeCurriculumModuleRecordsToDisplay=5\n#homeFlaggedCatalogItemsToDisplay specifies the maximum number of flagged items and programs to display for EACH category (e.g. max 25 New, max 25 Revised, and max 25 Featured)\nhomeFlaggedCatalogItemsToDisplay=25\n#\n### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Catalog Settings ***\n#\n#\n### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Competency Search Settings ***\n#\n#This configuration is used for controlling whether on the competency search screen, users by default see all courses they have access to that are tied to the specified competencies, or\n#just the courses that match or exceed their current competency rating.\n#False: Users first see just the courses that match or exceed their current competency rating. View only items that help me close competency gaps is enabled by default on the competency search screen.\n#True: Users first see all courses they have access to that are tied to the specified competencies.View only items that help me close competency gaps is disabled by default on the competency search screen.\nshowAllCoursesByDefault=false\n#\n### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Calendar Settings ***\n#\n#\n### **** End User Interaction Behavior: Persistence/Preferences ***\n#\n# Specify if the persistence can be lazy (does not have to happen immediately) and what class manages it. Default: true\nstudentSubordinatesLazyPersistence=true\nstudentSubordinatesPreferencesHandler=com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.StudentSubordinatesUIPreferencesHandler\n# The handler class that persists UI state preferences related to the user.\n# Default: com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.StudentUIPreferencesHandler\nstudentUIPreferencesHandler=com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.StudentUIPreferencesHandler\n# When set to true the Show Pictures checkbox on the Dashboard / Succession Planner is selected by default.\n# If hideUserPhotosGlobally is set to true, then ShowPictures is irrelevant. Default: true\nstudentSubordinatesShowPictures=true\n# When set to true the Show Status checkbox on Dashboard / Succession Planner is selected by default. Default: true\nstudentSubordinatesShowStatus=true\n#\n### ***** End User Interaction Behavior: Icon Preference ***\n#\n# Controls the icon preference on the end user interface. Default: true\nenableFontIcons=true\n#\n### ***** End User Interaction Behavior: Miscellaneous ***\n#\n# This setting determines if the competency type is displayed to the user when competencies are displayed.\nshowCompetencyType=true\n# talent search: max number of students per group\ntalentPoolMaxGroupSize=1000\n# This setting indicates the number of days from the current date to search for a new posts in the communities the user has access to.\n# This setting is used on the user's home page in the Communities button. Valid values are zero and any value greater than zero.\nsearchNewPostsToCommunitiesInTheLastDays=14\n# This setting would turn on or off the display of revision date time and number for items on the User's To-Do List.\ndisplayRevisionInformationInToDoList=false\n# This value is the number of reporting levels down displayed to a user and\n# should be an integer equal to or greater than 0.\n# Default: 0\n# Example:\n#   If set to 0, the user will see all direct and indirect subordinates.\n#   If set to 1, the user will see their direct reports only.\n#   If set to 2, the user will see their direct reports and direct reports reporting into their direct reports and so on\nreportingLevelsToDisplay=0\n# This configuration controls the display of the News page upon Login. Valid values are below (Values are case-sensitive):\n# Never : News page would not display on login. user would still have the ability to get to news page from the Easy link menu\n# Always : News page would always display on user login. User cannot dismiss this\n# UserDiscretion : News page would display upon login and the user would have the ability to not display each time. This is the default value\ndisplayNewsPageOnLogin=UserDiscretion\n# **********************************************************\n# ******** ADMIN/APPLICATION INTERACTION SETTINGS **********\n# **********************************************************\n#\n### **** Admin Application UI Behavior Configuration: Sticky Preferences ****\n#\n# Specify if the persistence can be lazy (does not have to happen immediately). Default: true\nuserUILazyPersistence=true\n# This section is used for setting the handler class that will persist UI state preferences related to Tab Modes.\n# Default: com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.UserUIPreferencesHandler\nuserUIPreferencesHandler=com.plateausystems.elms.client.state.impl.UserUIPreferencesHandler\n# Defaults the administrator's view of users' learning plans. Administrator can set own preference. If the option is true\n# then, by default, dates are displayed in the User's preferred time zone. If false, it is displayed in the Admin's preferred time zone. Default: true\nlearningPlanDisplayInLearnerTimezone=true\n#\n### **** Admin Application UI Behavior Configuration: Limits ****\n#\n# The maximum rating an administrator is allowed to give a learning item.\n# Admins assign ratings on the Item Summary tab and can appear to end users in catalog.\n# Whether or not ratings appear in the catalog is controlled by the showItemRatingInCatalog property (CatalogConfiguration).\nmaxItemRatingValue=5.0\n# Limits the amount of copies that the Copy Scheduled Offering Wizard can make in the Admin Environment.\n# Limit applies to the amount of copies the admin can make any ONE time they run the wizard.\n# Setting a reasonable limit prevents admins from mistakenly overwhelming database. Default: 50\nscheduleCopiesLimit=50\n# Limits the amount of \"recents\" entries that can be seen on the Admin Recents Panel\n# Setting a reasonable limit prevents admins from overwhelming database.\n# Default Value\t: 50 / Min Value: 1 / Max Value: 100\nmaxNumberOfRecentsDisplayed=50\n#\n### **** Admin Application UI Behavior Configuration: Security/Self Modification ***\n# When restrictUserSelfModification is set to \"true\" administrators cannot change their own records.\n# For example, when set to true, an administrator \"jdoe\" with permissions to change administrator accounts,\n# can change all other administrator password and permissions *except* for his own.\n# Default value is true. We recommend true. Possible values are true or false. You might set to\n# false in development or training environments, for convenience.\nrestrictUserSelfModification=true\n#\n### **** User E-Signature PIN Self Reset Configuration ***\n# This configuration determines whether learners can reset their E-Signature PIN if they forget it.\n# By default, the property is set to true. When true, learners can use \"Forgot My PIN\" on the \"Options and Settings\" page to receive a secure email link, allowing them to create a new PIN.\n# When set to false, the \"Forgot My PIN\" option is hidden.\nenableESignatureResetPIN=true\n# This flag is used to order module tabs alphabetically. By default, it is true and module tabs will be displayed in alphabetical order\n# except for the Summary tab. Setting it to false will result in module tabs being ordered as they historically have been before this\n# configuration was introduced.\ndisplayModuleTabsInAlphabeticalOrder=true\n#This flag is used to enable the new supervisor enhancements for Assign/Remove learning, Record learning and Register/Witdraw Users.\n#The Old supervisor flow is deprecated.\n#Configuration options: true is the only valid option\nupdatedSupervisorFlow=true\n#The maximum number of Users a Supervisor can register or withdraw using the Register / Withdraw Employees Wizard. The minimum value can be 1 and the maximum can be 1000.\nsupervisorMaxUserRegisterWithdrawLimit=50\n#This flag is used to enable the new tool for user Record learning.\n#The Old Self Record Learning flow is deprecated.\n#Configuration options: true is the only valid option\nupdatedSelfRecordLearningFlow=true\n# **************************************************************************************************\n# WARNING: No Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) filtering will be done if the URL is specified here as \"true\".\n# It is strongly recommended that you consult Plateau before modifying these values.\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/globalErrorDispatcher.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editAppAdminStudent.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateAppAdminStudent.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateConfiguration.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editConfigurationSummary.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateSearchSelector.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editSearchSelector.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateUIDataSummary.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editUIDataSummary.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/addUIDataSummary.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/showSystemConfigurationReport.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/editPrintedExamTemplate.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/updatePrintedExamTemplate.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/getSecurityQuestion.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/references/updateOrg.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/references/editOrg.do]=true\n# XSS filtering for Notification Template messages can be turned on/off using the WEB_SECURITY configuration setting enableXSSFiltersForNotificationTemplateMessages.\n# The settings in this block control whether XSS filtering is applied to URLs related to Notification Template messages.\n# When these URLs are excluded from XSS filtering (=true), Notification Template messages will allow inclusion of IMG tags and special characters.\n# When these URLs are included in XSS filtering (=false), inclusion of IMG tags and special characters is disallowed.\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/previewNotificationTemplateMessages.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/updateNotificationTemplateMessages.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/editNotificationTemplateMessages.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/listLabelNotificationTemplate.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/sysadmin/addNotificationTemplateMessage.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/sendNotificationAssistantStep5.do]=true\nxssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/student/previewCertificateOfCompletion.do]=true\n# Enable to allow admin update locale labels with such as <li> html tags, when for instance the\n# secRules.specialCharsNotAllowed.enabled XSS filter is turned on.\n#xssFilterExcludedURLs[/admin/tools/updateI18nActiveLocaleLabel.do]=true\n#request URL endings which can qualify the requests to be scanned\nxssFilterURLSuffix[.jsp]=true\n# These URLs which are outside of the regular *.jsp and *.do also need to be scanned\nxssFilterAdditionalURLs[/admin_acegi_authenticate]=true\nxssFilterAdditionalURLs[/student_acegi_authenticate]=true\nxssFilterAdditionalURLs[/site_acegi_authenticate]=true\n# Sets the login page behaviour to-remember or not-to-remember login crendentials.\n# Possible values are true/false.\nautoCompleteLoginForUser=true\nautoCompleteLoginForAdmin=true\n# This configuration is used to enable the online content early launch warning. This configuration\n# is added in b1207\n# true: will enable the early launch warning.\n# false: will disable the early launch warning.\nenableOnlineContentEarlyLaunchWarning=true\n#This configuration specifies the threshold for online content launch warning and is only\n#applicable when the \"enableOnlineContentEarlyLaunchWarning\" is set to true.\n# The value is number of days and should be a positive integer greater than or equal to 0.\nonlineContentEarlyLaunchWarningThreshold=45\n# **************************************************************************************************\n# Opted in Features Related Settings\n# **************************************************************************************************\n# This configuration is used to determine whether to use default password functionality or new initial random password generation. Added in b1207\n# true: will enable random password generation for all the users created in our system.\n# false: will use default password functionality.\nenableRandomPasswordGenerationForNewUsers=false\n# This configuration is used to enable item and program recommendations feature. This is added in b1207\n# true: will enable item and program recommedations feature.\n# false: will disable item and program recommendations feature.\nenableItemRecommendations=true\n# This configuration enforces the security domain restrictions set for the Edit Class permission when marking class attendance. The default value is false.\n# When set to true, any security domain restrictions for the Edit Class permission apply to marking class attendance. Only administrators with the necessary security domain permissions can mark attendance for classes.\n# When set to false, the security domain restrictions for the Edit Class permission don't apply to marking class attendance. Administrators with the Edit Class permission can mark attendance for classes, regardless of the configured security domain permissions.\nenforceSecurityDomainRestrictionForMarkingAttendance=false\n# **************************************************************************************************\n# Peer Recommendation settings\n# **************************************************************************************************\n# The Peer Recommendation would be hidden after the user has viewed the recommendation by navigating\n# to the Item / Program details page from the Recommendation tile and the entity has been added\n# to the Learning Plan or is part of the Learning History. This is to make the behavior\n# consistent with the Admin recommendations\n# This setting is deprecated and no longer used as of the 2H 2023 release.\nhideViewedP2PRecommendations=true\n# This configuration is the number of days after which a Peer Recommendation is deleted from the system.\n# After the number of configured days, a peer recommendation that has not been removed by the recipient will no longer appear in the peer recommendation section of the application.\n# The default value is 365 days. You can enter a value for this property only between 30 and 730 days. Revise the value to continue.\npeerRecommendationExpiration=365\n# This configuration is used to choose the type of links to be included in the notification email. This is a system level configuration that is to be chosen based on the level of authentication needed. This is added in b1505\n# true: will enable SmartLinks with personalized tokens for users to provide access without a login.\n# false: will provide a directlink to the recommended external link that requires a login to authenticate the user.\nenableSmartLinks=true\n# This configuration is used to enable multiple security questions for a user. This is added in b1210\nenableMultipleSecurityQuestionsForUser=false\n# This configuration will enable or disable offline login page.\nofflinePlayerLoginRequired=true\n# This configuration controls whether Offline Player can be upgraded by users.\n# Warning: If this configuration is set to false, users will not be able to download the Offline Player from Options and Settings.\nofflinePlayerUpgradeEnabled=true\n#Local offline url for communications\nofflinePlayerLocalUrl=http://localhost:53759/learningoffline\n# If showItemThumbnailPhotosGlobally is set to false, the Thumbnail File and Thumbnail URL fields will be hidden from the admin interface for Item and Program records. If set to true, the thumbnail fields are displayed on the admin interface which allows an admin to override the system default for a specific Item or Program; Item also requires the fields to be displayed on the record configuration. Default: false\nshowItemThumbnailPhotosGlobally=true\n# This configuration is used to determine maximum number of seats a supervisor can reserve while adding/editing a training requesting. Default: 500\n# Setting a reasonable limit prevents admins from overwhelming database.\n# Default Value\t: 500 / Min Value: 1 / Max Value: 10000\nmaxNumberOfTrainingRequestSeats=100\n# This configuration enables automatic assignment of training requests if the organization has been reviewed and either the seats requested equals seats granted\n# or the preselected user count is equal or less than the seats granted. Default: false. Possible values true/false\nautoAssignReviewedTrainingRequests=false\n# This configuration is used during the auto assignments of training requests, if the default assignment type is not provided for the items\ndefaultAssignmentTypeForAutoAssignTrainingRequests=\n# showSystemDefaultThumbnail decides whether the default thumbnail style is a photo (true) or an icon (false). Note that the system default thumbnail can be overridden for most learning at System Admin>Configuration>Images.\nshowSystemDefaultThumbnail=true\n# This configuration is used to enable HTML descriptions. Default: false\nenableHTMLDescriptions=true\n# Setting the allowFutureHireDates property to true enables the creation/update of user records with a future hire date. Default: false\n# Setting it back to false prevents the creation/update of user records with a future hire date but does not perform any data cleanup on existing records.\nallowFutureHireDates=false\n# Setting the enableCappingFactor to true enables Capping Factor feature.This will make the learning event recorder to display system default currency instead of the drop-down.It wont allow to change the currency for addition costs in Learning Event Editor. This will also hide Training days while recording learning. Default: false\nenableCappingFactor=false\n# This configuration is used to enable/disable the notification header and footer support.\nenableNotificationHeaderFooter=false\n# This configuration is used to set the maximum number of days that an admin is able to download their export\n# file results in the data export tool.  After the number of configured days, the admin will no longer be able\n# to access the export results. The allowable range is between 1-30 days.  Recommended default setting is 3.\nexportExpiration=3\n# This flag is used to allow if admins can enter/modify data in the registration form custom columns when registering/modifying users enrollment\nallowAdminToModifyRegistrationFormCustomColumns=true\nallowSupervisorToEnterRegistrationFormCustomColumnsData=true\nallowUserToModifyCustomColumnsDataIfRegisteredBySuper=false\nallowUserToModifyCustomColumnsDataIfRegisteredByAdmin=false\n# This configuration specifies the maximum number of subordinates displayed under any node, including the top-level nodes when displaying employees in the \"My Team\" tree-view\nmaxNumberOfSubordinatesDisplayedInTree=300\n# The following configuration allows the admin to identify whether or not users can submit incomplete surveys for surveys that are set as \"optional\". This setting applies to\n# both Item Evaluation and Follow-up Evaluation survey types\nUsersCanSubmitIncompleteOptionalSurveys=false\n#Enables the Manage Learning Tool from a scheduled offering.\nmanageLearningToolEnabled=false\n# This configuration allows the publishing of events to the Service Event Bus (SEB) to be enabled or disabled, based on the SEB-supported event type.\n#If the destination is unavailable at the time the event is published to the SEB, the event publication fails. You can enable rerunFailedSebPublishedEvents to process the failed events from previous days. You can rerun events for up to 30 days prior to the current day. The number of prior days to reprocess is set in numberOfPriorDaysToRerunSebPublishedEvents.\nsebPublishedEventTypes[LearningCompletion]=false\nrerunFailedSebPublishedEvents=false\nnumberOfPriorDaysToRerunSebPublishedEvents=1\n# When set to true, if a self-registering user provides an email address, the system will not register the user unless that email address is unique across all users of the system\nselfRegistrationUniqueEmailAddressRequired=false\n# This configuration can be used to indicate whether the LMS instance is integrated with Jam or not.\n# (Note: this property replaces the previously used 'enableSocialTabInCatalogSearch' property.)\n# true: Indicates that Jam integration available and enabled\n# false: Indicates that Jam integration is not available or disabled\njamIntegrationEnabled=false\n#When set to true, the from field of the email notification will be replaced with the the recipient's org email.\nuseOrgEmailAsFromForNotifications=false\n#This configuration is dependent on Course Home being enabled (enableCourseHomeBlended=true).\n#When set to true, content will always launch inline, regardless of the content-level setting.\n#When set to false, the content-level setting determines the launch method.\n#Default value is false.\noverrideContentLaunchInNewWindow=false\n#This configuration will enable the content object Audit\n#When set to true , new field(enable_content_audit) is visible on item snapshot for online and blended courses\n#when enable_content_audit is set to true , the content communication is saved to Audit table i.e., PA_CBT_STUD_CPNT_MOD_AUDIT\nenableContentObjectAuditTrail=false\n# This property applies to the new Learning experience to show or hide the Required Learning section. The default value is set to false.\n# If no required courses are assigned to users, and you want to hide the section for them, set the property to true. This property applies to specific organizations and user groups where the section is set to be hidden.\n#When hideRequiredLearningSectionOnLearningPortal is set to true, users do not see the Required Learning section on their Learning Portal. Note that when there is content on the Required Learning section, setting the property to true does not hide the section on users' Learning Portal.\n#When hideRequiredLearningSectionOnLearningPortal is set to false, the Required Learning section appears on the users' Learning Portal.\nhideRequiredLearningSectionOnLearningPortal=false\n# When this configuration is enabled, the Purge Deleted User Audit\n# History APM will add a list of the purged users to PA_USER_PURGE_LOG.\n# Disabling this configuration does not delete any previously added records.\n# WARNING: Enabling purge logging will prevent reusing a purged User ID in the future.\nenablePurgeLog=false\n# This KBA feature depends on the System Setting enableErrorFingerprinting JVM flag.\n# If the enableErrorFingerprinting flag is false, this setting will be considered as false always.\n# Set it to false to opt out\nenableKBASearchService=true\n# When this configuration is enabled, the user can view the Learning History of all Employments.\n# Set the learningHistoryOfAllEmployments flag as false to opt out.\nlearningHistoryOfAllEmployments=false\n# For customers integrated with Talent Intelligence Hub, setting this configuration to true allows users to view the legacy 'Competencies' entity in the menu, in addition to the 'Attributes' entity.\n# The competency search selector functionality remains the same.\nshowCompetenciesMenuAfterTalentIntelligenceHubMigration=false\n#This configuration prevents intermittent early completion issues for SCORM 2004 4th edition content that occur when a learner navigates away from or exits content.\n#When set to true, this configuration assumes that the completionSetByContent and objectiveSetByContent values in the content manifest are true, so Learning records completion only after the content communicates completion.\n#The default value is false and the setting values in the content manifest determine how content completion is communicated.\ncontentCommunicatesCompletion=true\n#This configuration allows the continued use of unload browser events for online content and is enabled (true) by default.\n# This temporary setting is intended to allow customers additional time to replace unload browser events for their online content and will only be available until Google deprecates support in 2025.\nenableContentUnloadEventUsage=true\n#This configuration is specific to ILX and decides the behaviour of primary actions related to Launch Course on ILX cards\n#When set to true, the primary actions related to Launch Course would redirect to Course Home page.\n#When set to false, the primary actions related to Launch Course would redirect directly to Course Launch.\nnavigateToCourseHomeForILXLaunchCourseActions=false\n#The configuration determines whether additional details for learning cards, such as learning ID, rating, description, associated skills, and other metadata, are shown in the \"Details\" popover when a learner selects a learning card on the new Learning home page.\n#The default is set to true, where the \"Details\" popover appears with the additional information for a learning.\n#When set to false, learners are redirected to the \"Course Home\" page, without displaying the popover.\ndisplayAdditionalDetailsForLearningCards=true\n#The configuration determines whether deleting iContent files using the iContent Management tool also removes the content structure from its linked courses. The default value is set to false.\n#When set to false, deleting files retains the content structure in all associated courses. You need to manually remove the deleted content from the structure and reactivate the course.\n#When set to true, deleting files automatically removes the content structure from all associated courses. While the remaining content is still accessible, it is no longer linked to the course.\nremoveContentStructureOnDelete=false\n#The configuration determines whether learners can access the redesigned \"Program Details\", \"Curriculum Details\" and \"Curricula Status\" pages from the Learning home page.\n#The default is false where learners continue to access the legacy pages.\n#Set it to true for learners to access the redesigned pages.\nenableLegacyUIReplacement=true\n\n# This configuration controls whether the user should be allowed to access course in a program which has approvals.\n# When set to false (default), users are not restricted from accessing courses in programs with approvals.\n# When set to true, the system enforces approval requirements for accessing courses in programs.\nhonorApprovalsForPrograms=true\n\n# This configuration controls whether the system honors prerequisites when managing learning programs.\n# When set to true, the system enforces prerequisite requirements for program enrollment and completion.\n# When set to false, prerequisite enforcement is disabled, allowing users to access programs without meeting prerequisites.\nhonorPrerequisitesForPrograms=true"}}]}}